{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788201473681,"sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_3a69113d58e04319b4d301e5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef load(path):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\n# BR-Football seasons per tournament\nrows = load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nfor t in ['Serie A','Serie B','Serie C','Copa do Brasil']:\n    seasons = sorted(set(r['date'][:4] for r in rows if r['tournament']==t))\n    print(t, \"seasons:\", seasons)\n\n# check overlap: Brasileirao_Matches 2012-2019 vs novo 2012-2019\nbm = load('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nnv = load('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nbm_keys = set((r['datetime'][:10], r['home_team'], r['away_team']) for r in bm if r['season']<='2019')\nnv_keys = set((r['Data'][6:]+'-'+r['Data'][3:5]+'-'+r['Data'][:2], r['Equipe_mandante'], r['Equipe_visitante']) for r in nv if r['Ano']>='2012')\nprint(\"\\nBrasileirao_Matches 2012-19 keys:\", len(bm_keys), \" novo 2012-19 keys:\", len(nv_keys))\ninter = bm_keys & nv_keys\nprint(\"exact-date overlaps:\", len(inter))\n# sample differences\ndiff_bm = list(bm_keys - nv_keys)[:3]\nprint(\"only in BM:\", diff_bm)\ndiff_nv = list(nv_keys - bm_keys)[:3]\nprint(\"only in novo:\", diff_nv)\n\n# BR-Football Serie A vs Brasileirao_Matches overlap\nbrfa = set((r['date'], r['home'], r['away']) for r in rows if r['tournament']=='Serie A')\nprint(\"\\nBR-Football Serie A sample:\", sorted(brfa)[:3])\nprint(\"BR-Football Serie A years:\", sorted(set(k[0][:4] for k in brfa)))\nEOF","workdir":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5"},"output":"Serie A seasons: ['2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021', '2022', '2023']\nSerie B seasons: ['2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021', '2022', '2023']\nSerie C seasons: ['2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021', '2022', '2023']\nCopa do Brasil seasons: ['2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021', '2022', '2023']\n\nBrasileirao_Matches 2012-19 keys: 3040  novo 2012-19 keys: 3040\nexact-date overlaps: 0\nonly in BM: [('2018-07-29', 'Santos-SP', 'America-MG'), ('2016-10-29', 'Figueirense-SC', 'Gremio-RS'), ('2016-06-18', 'Atletico-PR', 'Santos-SP')]\nonly in novo: [('2018-06-10', 'Corinthians', 'Vitória'), ('2016-05-25', 'Coritiba', 'São Paulo'), ('2018-05-27', 'América-MG', 'São Paulo')]\n\nBR-Football Serie A sample: [('2014-06-05', 'Sport Recife', 'EC Bahia'), ('2014-07-16', 'Gremio', 'Goias'), ('2014-07-16', 'Sport Recife', 'Botafogo RJ')]\nBR-Football Serie A years: ['2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021', '2022', '2023']\n","metadata":{"output":"Serie A seasons: ['2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021', '2022', '2023']\nSerie B seasons: ['2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021', '2022', '2023']\nSerie C seasons: ['2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021', '2022', '2023']\nCopa do Brasil seasons: ['2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021', '2022', '2023']\n\nBrasileirao_Matches 2012-19 keys: 3040  novo 2012-19 keys: 3040\nexact-date overlaps: 0\nonly in BM: [('2018-07-29', 'Santos-SP', 'America-MG'), ('2016-10-29', 'Figueirense-SC', 'Gremio-RS'), ('2016-06-18', 'Atletico-PR', 'Santos-SP')]\nonly in novo: [('2018-06-10', 'Corinthians', 'Vitória'), ('2016-05-25', 'Coritiba', 'São Paulo'), ('2018-05-27', 'América-MG', 'São Paulo')]\n\nBR-Football Serie A sample: [('2014-06-05', 'Sport Recife', 'EC Bahia'), ('2014-07-16', 'Gremio', 'Goias'), ('2014-07-16', 'Sport Recife', 'Botafogo RJ')]\nBR-Football Serie A years: ['2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021', '2022', '2023']\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef load(path):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\n# BR-Football seasons per tournament\nrows = load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nfor t in ['Serie A','Serie B','Serie C','Copa do Brasil']:\n    seasons = sorted(set(r['date'][:4] for r in rows if r['tournament']==t))\n    print(t, \"seasons:\", seasons)\n\n# check overlap: Brasileirao_Matches 2012-2019 vs novo 2012-2019\nbm = load('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nnv = load('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nbm_keys = set((r['datetime'][:10], r['home_team'], r['away_team']) for r in bm if r['season']<='2019')\nnv_keys = set((r['Data'][6:]+'-'+r['Data'][3:5]+'-'+r['Data'][:2], r['Equipe_mandante'], r['Equipe_visitante']) for r in nv if r['Ano']>='2012')\nprint(\"\\nBrasileirao_Matches 2012-19 keys:\", len(bm_keys), \" novo 2012-19 keys:\", len(nv_keys))\ninter = bm_keys & nv_keys\nprint(\"exact-date overlaps:\", len(inter))\n# sample differences\ndiff_bm = list(bm_keys - nv_keys)[:3]\nprint(\"only in BM:\", diff_bm)\ndiff_nv = list(nv_keys - bm_keys)[:3]\nprint(\"only in novo:\", diff_nv)\n\n# BR-Football Serie A vs Brasileirao_Matches overlap\nbrfa = set((r['date'], r['home'], r['away']) for r in rows if r['tournament']=='Serie A')\nprint(\"\\nBR-Football Serie A sample:\", sorted(brfa)[:3])\nprint(\"BR-Football Serie A years:\", sorted(set(k[0][:4] for k in brfa)))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788201473673,"end":1788201473679}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I have a good understanding of the data. Let me check team name variations across the datasets to design a normalization function. Key challenges:\n\n1. **Brasileirao_Matches.csv**: \"Palmeiras-SP\", \"Flamengo-RJ\" (ASCII, no accents — \"Atletico-MG\" not \"Atlético-MG\", \"Avai-SC\")\n2. **Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv**: \"América - MG\" (with accents), \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\"\n3. **Libertadores_Matches.csv**: \"Barcelona-EQU\", \"Nacional (URU)\" — includes non-Brazilian teams\n4. **BR-Football-Dataset.csv**: \"Sao Paulo\", \"Flamengo\" (no state, ASCII)\n5. **novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv**: \"Guarani\", \"Grêmio\", \"Athletico-PR\" (with accents)\n6. **fifa_data.csv**: \"Grêmio\", \"Atlético Mineiro\", \"Atlético Paranaense\", \"Sport Club do Recife\", \"Ceará Sporting Club\", \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\"\n\nSo normalization needs to:\n- Strip state suffixes: \"-SP\", \" - RJ\", \"(URU)\", \"-EQU\"\n- Remove accents (NFD normalization)\n- Lowercase\n- Handle common name variations: \"Atletico-MG\" vs \"Atlético Mineiro\" vs \"Atlético Paranaense\" vs \"Athletico-PR\"\n\nTricky cases:\n- \"Atletico-MG\" (Brasileirao) vs \"Atlético Mineiro\" (FIFA) — need alias mapping\n- \"Atletico-PR\" (Brasileirao) vs \"Athletico-PR\" (novo) vs \"Atlético Paranaense\" (FIFA)\n- \"America-MG\" vs \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" vs \"América - MG\"\n- \"Ceara-CE\" vs \"Ceará Sporting Club\"\n- \"Sport-PE\" vs \"Sport Club do Recife\"\n- \"Avai-SC\" vs \"Avaí\"\n- \"Sao Paulo\" vs \"São Paulo\"\n\nLet me look at all the unique team names in the smaller datasets to build good aliases. Let me also check what Brazilian teams appear in Libertadores.\n\nAlso there's a subtlety: \"Atletico-MG\" and \"Atletico-PR\" and \"Atletico-GO\" — stripping the suffix gives \"atletico\" for all three, which would collide! So I can't just strip suffixes blindly — \"Atletico-MG\" minus state is \"atletico\" but there are three distinct Atleticos. The state is a disambiguator. So normalization should keep the state when the base name alone is ambiguous.\n\nApproach: normalize name → canonical key that includes state when needed:\n- \"Palmeiras-SP\" → \"palmeiras\"\n- \"Atletico-MG\" → \"atletico-mg\" (keep state)\n- \"Atlético Mineiro\" → \"atletico-mg\" (alias mapping)\n- \"Atlético Paranaense\" / \"Athletico-PR\" / \"Atletico-PR\" → \"atletico-pr\"\n- \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → \"atletico... no → \"america-mg\"\n\nLet me enumerate all unique team names across datasets first.\n\nAlso for matching user queries like \"Flamengo\", I need fuzzy resolution: \"Flamengo\" matches \"Flamengo-RJ\", \"Flamengo\". And \"Corinthians\" → \"Corinthians-SP\" → \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\".\n\nPlan for architecture:\n\n```\n.\n├── TASK.md (existing)\n├── README.md (update at end)\n├── requirements.txt\n├── pyproject.toml (maybe)\n├── src/ or flat?\n```\n\nGiven \"Write all code files to the current directory\", I'll structure as a package:\n\n```\nbrasileirao_mcp/  (or brazilian_soccer_mcp)\n├── __init__.py\n├── models.py        # dataclasses: Match, Player, TeamRecord\n├── normalize.py     # team name normalization + alias resolution\n├── loader.py        # CSV loading, date parsing, all 6 datasets\n├── queries.py       # query engine: match/team/player/competition/stats\n├── server.py        # MCP server exposing tools (mcp SDK, stdio)\n└── cli.py?          # maybe a direct query CLI for testing\ntests/\n├── conftest.py\n├── test_bdd_match_queries.py (GWT-style BDD tests)\n├── test_bdd_team_queries.py\n├── test_bdd_player_queries.py\n├── test_bdd_competition_queries.py\n├── test_bdd_statistics.py\n└── test_server.py   # MCP server tool tests\n```\n\nThe TASK.md testing approach says: Use BDD test scenarios — Gherkin Given/When/Then structured PyTest. So tests should be structured with Given/When/Then comments and test names.\n\nMCP server tools to expose:\n1. `search_matches(team=?, opponent=?, competition=?, season=?, date_from=?, date_to=?, stage=?, limit=?)` — match queries\n2. `head_to_head(team_a, team_b, competition=?, limit=?)` — H2H records\n3. `team_stats(team, season=?, competition=?, home_away=?)` — W/D/L, goals\n4. `standings(season, competition=?)` — calculated league table\n5. `search_players(name=?, nationality=?, club=?, position=?, min_rating=?, order_by=?, limit=?)` — player queries\n6. `club_players(club)` — players at a club\n7. `top_scorers`? Not inferable per player, but \"biggest wins\" and \"average goals\" are stats:\n8. `statistics(competition=?, season=?)` — avg goals/match, home win rate\n9. `biggest_wins(competition=?, limit=?)`\n10. `list_teams(competition=?)` / `list_competitions()` — discovery helpers\n11. `find_team(name)` — resolve team name variations to canonical names\n\nAlso \"derbies\" — matches between traditional rivals. I can implement a derbies tool: known derby pairs (Fla-Flu, Gre-Nal, Clássico dos Milhões, Choque-Rei, Majestoso, etc.), find matches between them.\n\nLet me design the data model:\n\n**Match** dataclass:\n- date: date | None\n- home_team: str (display name)\n- away_team: str\n- home_goals: int | None\n- away_goals: int | None\n- competition: str (canonical: \"Brasileirão\", \"Copa do Brasil\", \"Copa Libertadores\", \"Serie B\", \"Serie C\", ...)\n- season: int | None\n- round: str | None\n- stage: str | None\n- venue: str | None (novo has Arena)\n- state fields maybe\n\n**Player** dataclass:\n- id, name, age, nationality, overall, potential, club, position, jersey, preferred_foot, value, wage, height, weight, skill ratings dict\n\nCompetition naming: I'll unify:\n- Brasileirao_Matches.csv → \"Brasileirão\" (Serie A 2012-2022)\n- novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv → \"Brasileirão\" (2003-2019) — same competition, historical. So both map to competition \"Brasileirão\" but different seasons mostly. There's overlap 2012-2019 between the two files! Both have 2012-2019 Brasileirão. Hmm — duplicates? Let me check: Brasileirao_Matches has 2012-2022 (4180 matches = 11 seasons × 380). novo has 2003-2019 (6886 matches = 17 seasons, ~380-400 each). So 2012-2019 overlap = duplicated data in two files. For queries across the whole dataset, that means Flamengo 2012-2019 matches would appear twice unless deduplicated.\n\nDedup strategy: keep matches from both files but mark source; for aggregate queries maybe dedupe by (date, home, away)? The two datasets may have slightly different dates. Actually for the \"Brasileirão\" competition I could prefer one source per season. Let me check overlap more carefully.\n\nActually simpler and defensible: treat both files as sources of Brasileirão matches; deduplicate exact matches (same date+teams+score). If dates differ slightly between sources, there'd be some dupes left. Let me check.\n\nLet me also check BR-Football-Dataset \"Serie A\" — which seasons? It has 3689 Serie A matches. Dates from 2023 backwards? Let me check season range. This dataset covers 2012-2023 maybe with Serie A/B/C. So Brasileirão Serie A would also overlap with BR-Football Serie A! Need to check.\n\nFor standings calculation, \"Who won the 2019 Brasileirão\" — I should calculate from match data. 2019 is in both Brasileirao_Matches and novo. If I dedupe, standings would be right (38 rounds × 10 matches = 380 matches per season for 20 teams).\n\nLet me check the overlap situation between the datasets.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0591d161e001U5sXFLLtHwhbbn","sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","messageID":"msg_0591c7429001uwdrAqwYn6gCrh"}}
