{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788201487786,"sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_68f29128330e41f78587ae00","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, unicodedata\n\ndef strip_accents(s):\n    return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFD', s) if unicodedata.category(c) != 'Mn')\n\ndef norm(name):\n    n = strip_accents(name).lower()\n    # strip state suffix like -SP, -RJ\n    import re\n    n = re.sub(r'[-\\s]\\s*[a-z]{2}$', '', n) if n.count('-') <= 1 else n\n    return n.strip()\n\ndef load(path):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nbm = load('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nnv = load('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nbm_keys = set((r['datetime'][:10], norm(r['home_team']), norm(r['away_team'])) for r in bm if r['season']<='2019')\nnv_keys = set((r['Data'][6:]+'-'+r['Data'][3:5]+'-'+r['Data'][:2], norm(r['Equipe_mandante']), norm(r['Equipe_visitante'])) for r in nv if r['Ano']>='2012')\nprint(\"overlap after norm:\", len(bm_keys & nv_keys), \"of\", len(bm_keys), \"/\", len(nv_keys))\n\n# check score agreement on overlaps\nbm_scores = {}\nfor r in bm:\n    bm_scores[(r['datetime'][:10], norm(r['home_team']), norm(r['away_team']))] = (r['home_goal'], r['away_goal'])\nmism = 0\nfor k in (bm_keys & nv_keys):\n    if k in bm_scores: pass\nprint(\"sample intersection:\", list(bm_keys & nv_keys)[:3])\n\n# BR-Football Serie A overlap with BM after norm\nrows = load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nbrfa = set((r['date'], norm(r['home']), norm(r['away'])) for r in rows if r['tournament']=='Serie A')\nprint(\"BR-FA Serie A overlap with BM:\", len(brfa & bm_keys))\nEOF","workdir":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5"},"output":"overlap after norm: 2490 of 3040 / 3040\nsample intersection: [('2019-09-25', 'ceara', 'cruzeiro'), ('2014-11-16', 'internacional', 'goias'), ('2013-06-06', 'coritiba', 'fluminense')]\nBR-FA Serie A overlap with BM: 1126\n","metadata":{"output":"overlap after norm: 2490 of 3040 / 3040\nsample intersection: [('2019-09-25', 'ceara', 'cruzeiro'), ('2014-11-16', 'internacional', 'goias'), ('2013-06-06', 'coritiba', 'fluminense')]\nBR-FA Serie A overlap with BM: 1126\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, unicodedata\n\ndef strip_accents(s):\n    return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFD', s) if unicodedata.category(c) != 'Mn')\n\ndef norm(name):\n    n = strip_accents(name).lower()\n    # strip state suffix like -SP, -RJ\n    import re\n    n = re.sub(r'[-\\s]\\s*[a-z]{2}$', '', n) if n.count('-') <= 1 else n\n    return n.strip()\n\ndef load(path):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nbm = load('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nnv = load('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nbm_keys = set((r['datetime'][:10], norm(r['home_team']), norm(r['away_team'])) for r in bm if r['season']<='2019')\nnv_keys = set((r['Data'][6:]+'-'+r['Data'][3:5]+'-'+r['Data'][:2], norm(r['Equipe_mandante']), norm(r['Equipe_visitante'])) for r in nv if r['Ano']>='2012')\nprint(\"overlap after norm:\", len(bm_keys & nv_keys), \"of\", len(bm_keys), \"/\", len(nv_keys))\n\n# check score agreement on overlaps\nbm_scores = {}\nfor r in bm:\n    bm_scores[(r['datetime'][:10], norm(r['home_team']), norm(r['away_team']))] = (r['home_goal'], r['away_goal'])\nmism = 0\nfor k in (bm_keys & nv_keys):\n    if k in bm_scores: pass\nprint(\"sample intersection:\", list(bm_keys & nv_keys)[:3])\n\n# BR-Football Serie A overlap with BM after norm\nrows = load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nbrfa = set((r['date'], norm(r['home']), norm(r['away'])) for r in rows if r['tournament']=='Serie A')\nprint(\"BR-FA Serie A overlap with BM:\", len(brfa & bm_keys))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788201487779,"end":1788201487785}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting findings:\n\n1. Brasileirao_Matches (2012-2019) and novo (2012-2019) have the same 3040 matches but team names differ (\"Santos-SP\" vs \"Santos\") and apparently dates differ too — 0 exact overlaps on (date, home, away) with team names as-is. But when normalizing team names (strip -SP), the dates might match. Let me check with normalized names.\n\n2. BR-Football Serie A 2014-2022 also overlaps with Brasileirão Serie A. Team names differ again (\"Gremio\" vs \"Gremio-RS\", \"Sport Recife\" vs \"Sport-PE\").\n\nDedup approach: normalize team names, then dedupe on (date, home_norm, away_norm). If dates differ between sources (some datasets might have slightly different dates), there could still be dupes. Let me check with normalized team names whether dates match between BM and novo.\n\nActually, for a knowledge-graph style server, exact dedup across sources is less critical. But for standings calculation (who won 2019 Brasileirão), duplicated matches would corrupt the table. Approach for standings: prefer a single source per competition-season when available. Priority: use one designated primary source per (competition, season) for standings; e.g., for Brasileirão 2012-2019 prefer Brasileirao_Matches (has explicit round), 2003-2011 only in novo, 2020-2022 only in Brasileirao_Matches, 2023 only in BR-Football (Serie A).\n\nSimpler robust approach: build matches list with a \"source\" field; dedupe by (competition, season, normalized home, normalized away, date) — and if dates differ across sources for the same fixture... Let me check whether BM and novo matches match after team normalization on the same date.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0591d4d34001Gw1cMLJP1LY7JV","sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","messageID":"msg_0591d17dc0010DqUE1bA5zcLnz"}}
