ernacional: 20\n  Paraná: 20\n  Real Sporting de Gijón: 30\n  Santos: 20\n  Santos Laguna: 26\n  Sport Club do Recife: 20\n  Sporting CP: 30\n  Sporting Kansas City: 27\n  Sporting Lokeren: 28\n  Sporting de Charleroi: 28\n  VfL Sportfreunde Lotte: 28\n  Vitória: 20\n  Vitória Guimarães: 30\n  Vitória de Setúbal: 28\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef load(path):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nlib = load('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv')\nteams = set()\nfor r in lib:\n    teams.add(r['home_team']); teams.add(r['away_team'])\nbr = sorted(t for t in teams if 'BRA' in t or t in ('Palmeiras','Flamengo','Grêmio','Corinthians'))\nprint(\"Libertadores BRA-suffixed teams sample:\", br[:15])\nprint(\"Libertadores all teams count:\", len(teams))\nprint(\"sample of others:\", sorted(teams)[:15])\n\nfifa = load('data/kaggle/fifa_data.csv')\nclubs = Counter(r['Club'] for r in fifa if r['Club'])\n# find Brazilian-ish club names\nbrazilian_hint = ['Flamengo','Palmeiras','Corinthians','São Paulo','Sao Paulo','Vasco','Grêmio','Gremio','Internacional','Cruzeiro','Atlético','Athletico','Bahia','Sport','Ceará','Goiás','Fortaleza','Chapecoense','Vitória','América','Botafogo','Fluminense','Santos','Paraná','Avaí','Criciúma','Ponte Preta','Athletico Paranaense','Atlético Goianiense','Oeste','Boa','Operário']\nfound = [c for c in clubs if any(h in c for h in brazilian_hint)]\nprint(\"\\nFIFA Brazilian clubs:\")\nfor c in sorted(found):\n    print(f\"  {c}: {clubs[c]}\")\nEOF","time":{"start":1788201570064,"end":1788201570083}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"This confirms the design: I need a canonical key that keeps the state when the base name is ambiguous (e.g. \"atletico\" → \"atletico-mg\", \"atletico-pr\", \"atletico-go\", \"atletico-es\", \"atletico-ba\", \"atletico-ac\"; \"botafogo\" → rj/pb; \"flamengo\" → rj/pi; \"america\" → mg/rn; \"santos\" → sp/ap; etc.).\n\nCanonicalization strategy:\n1. Clean the raw name: strip \"(antigo ...)\" parenthetical, strip accents, lowercase.\n2. Extract trailing state suffix if present: \"-SP\", \" - RJ\", \"-EQU\", \" (URU)\" etc. Two-letter Brazilian state abbreviations (26 states + DF): AC, AL, AP, AM, BA, CE, DF, ES, GO, MA, MT, MS, MG, PA, PB, PR, PE, PI, RJ, RN, RS, RO, RR, SC, SP, SE, TO. For Libertadores, foreign teams have country suffixes: EQU (Ecuador), URU (Uruguay), ARG, CHI, COL, PAR, PER, VEN, BOL, MEX... I'll treat 3-letter foreign suffixes differently — strip them and keep the base name.\n3. If a state suffix is present: canonical = base + \"-\" + state (e.g., \"atletico-mg\"). If not present: canonical = base, UNLESS the base is ambiguous (belongs to multiple states), in which case... we can't disambiguate — e.g., FIFA \"Atlético Mineiro\" → alias to \"atletico-mg\".\n\nSo I need an explicit alias table for ambiguous base names to their canonical entries:\n- \"atletico mineiro\" → \"atletico-mg\"\n- \"atletico paranaense\"/\"athletico paranaense\"/\"paranaense\" → \"atletico-pr\"\n- FIFA club names: \"Atlético Mineiro\" → atletico-mg; \"Atlético Paranaense\" → atletico-pr; \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → america-mg; \"Ceará Sporting Club\" → ceara-ce; \"Sport Club do Recife\" → sport-pe; \"Sport Recife\" (BR-Football) → sport-pe; \"Botafogo RJ\"/\"Botafogo PB\"? BR-Football has \"Botafogo RJ\"? Let me check BR-Football unique names. Also \"EC Bahia\" → bahia-ba; \"Goias\" → goias-go; \"Avai\" → avai-sc; \"Coritiba\" → coritiba-pr; etc.\n\nFor ambiguous bases without state (e.g., plain \"Botafogo\" in FIFA — which one? Botafogo RJ has 20 players in FIFA; is there a Botafogo-PB in FIFA? Probably not). Heuristic: for ambiguous base names, if only ONE of the known state variants is \"major\" or the alias table maps it, use that; otherwise resolve at query time by preferring the most common variant in match data (most matches played). E.g., \"botafogo\" → botafogo-rj (RJ is the big club, most matches). \"flamengo\" → flamengo-rj. \"america\" → hmm, america-mg vs america-rn — ambiguous even in Brazil! In FIFA data there's \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" (MG). For plain \"America\" queries, most-matches heuristic: america-mg (Serie A) more matches than america-rn.\n\nThis heuristic is good: for a canonical-less base name that collides, pick the variant with the most matches in the dataset. This works for flamengo (rj >> pi), botafogo (rj >> pb), santos (sp >> ap), america (mg > rn), internacional (rs >> sc), sport (pe), nautico (pe >> rr), guarani (sp), ceara (ce), etc.\n\nBut careful — canonical storage: each match stores BOTH the display name and the canonical key. Canonical keys should retain state when the dataset provided it. For novo data (\"Corinthians\" without state) → canonical \"corinthians\" (base, unambiguous) — but BM has \"Corinthians-SP\" → canonical \"corinthians-sp\". These would be DIFFERENT keys for the same team! That breaks dedup and H2H across sources.\n\nSolution: canonical key must be fully normalized: for each base name that is ambiguous, ALL occurrences (with or without state) must map to the same key. For unambiguous bases, strip state entirely. So:\n- \"Corinthians-SP\" → \"corinthians\" (unambiguous base → drop state)\n- \"Corinthians\" → \"corinthians\"\n- \"Atletico-MG\" → \"atletico-mg\" (ambiguous base → keep state)\n- \"Atlético Mineiro\" → \"atletico-mg\" (via alias)\n- \"Atletico\" (no state, ambiguous) → needs disambiguation → alias table or most-matches.\n\nThe ambiguity set must be GLOBAL: computed from all names across all match datasets. E.g. \"santa cruz\" appears with PE, RN, RS → ambiguous; \"nautico\" RR/PE → ambiguous.\n\nHow do I compute ambiguity before loading? Two passes over the data at load time:\n- Pass 1: collect all (base → set of states) from match files.\n- Pass 2: canonicalize each team name: base + state if base ambiguous else base. Plus alias table applied first for full-name variants (e.g. \"atletico mineiro\" → base \"atletico\", state \"mg\").\n\nAlias table entries needed (name → (base, state)):\n- \"atletico mineiro\" → atletico/mg\n- \"atletico paranaense\"/\"athletico paranaense\" → atletico/pr\n- \"america fc (minas gerais)\" → america/mg  (FIFA)\n- \"ceara sporting club\" → ceara/ce (FIFA)\n- \"sport club do recife\" → sport/pe (FIFA)\n- \"sport recife\" → sport/pe (BR-Football)\n- \"ec bahia\" → bahia/ba (BR-Football)\n- \"botafogo rj\"? need to check BR-Football names\n- \"red bull brasil\" → bragantino? No — Red Bull Brasil is a different club from Red Bull Bragantino. Keep separate.\n- \"athletic club\"? not needed.\n- \"gremio\"/\"grêmio\" → gremio (unambiguous) fine.\n- \"sao paulo\" fine.\n- FIFA \"Atlético Goianiense\"? let me check FIFA Brazilian club list more fully.\n- \"parana\" → parana-pr fine if unambiguous.\n- \"coritiba\" fine.\n- \"bahia de feira\" fine.\n- \"vitoria\" → vitoria-ba (vs vitoria da conquista — different base, fine; but is \"vitoria\" ambiguous? only BA in list → unambiguous → \"vitoria\").\n- \"internacional\" ambiguous (rs/sc) → internacional-rs by most matches; FIFA \"Internacional\" → maps how? In pass 2, plain \"internacional\" is ambiguous-base-no-state → I need default resolution. Store the RAW canonical as \"internacional\" but resolve to most-matches at query time? That complicates matching (internacional-rs vs internacional keys differ).\n\nSimpler: at load time, resolve ambiguous-no-state names to the most-common state for that base (most matches across all files). So \"Internacional\" (FIFA, BR-Football, novo) → \"internacional-rs\". \"Botafogo\" (novo, FIFA) → \"botafogo-rj\". \"America\" → \"america-mg\". This is deterministic given the data. Edge: genuinely ambiguous clubs like America-MG vs América-RN — data has \"América - RN\" WITH state so it's preserved; only stateless \"America\" collapses to MG. Acceptable for a demo, and documented.\n\nHmm wait, but there's a subtlety with \"Sport-PE\" in BM vs \"Sport\" in novo vs \"Sport Club do Recife\" in FIFA vs \"Sport Recife\" in BR-Football: base \"sport\" appears only with PE → unambiguous → all become \"sport\". Good.\n\n\"Ceara-CE\", \"Ceará\", \"Ceará - CE\", \"Ceará Sporting Club\" → all \"ceara\". Good.\n\nNow FIFA club names — I need to map FIFA club names to canonical keys so cross-queries work (\"Which players play for Flamengo?\"). FIFA Brazilian clubs: Grêmio, Atlético Mineiro, Cruzeiro, Fluminense, Santos, Internacional, América FC (Minas Gerais), Botafogo, Bahia, Paraná, Atlético Paranaense, Vitória, Sport Club do Recife, Chapecoense, Ceará Sporting Club, ... let me enumerate all FIFA clubs that contain Brazilian clubs. There might also be \"Palmeiras\", \"Flamengo\", \"São Paulo\", \"Corinthians\", \"Vasco da Gama\", \"Goiás\", \"Fortaleza\", \"Athletico Paranaense\"? Let me check.\n\nAlso foreign suffixes in Libertadores: \"Barcelona-EQU\" (Ecuador), \"Nacional (URU)\", \"The Strongest (BOL)\", \"Palmeiras-BRA\"? Let me check Libertadores naming for Brazilian teams: probably \"Flamengo-BRA\"? Let me look.\n\nThen the query-resolution for user input: normalize user input → canonical key via same pipeline; if not found, fuzzy match (substring, startswith) against known canonical names + alias table. E.g. \"Flu\" → ? Probably too fuzzy; skip nicknames except a few well-known: \"Flu\" (Fluminense), \"Fla\" (Flamengo), \"Timão\" (Corinthians)? Keep it minimal: maybe include a few common nicknames in the alias table. Good for demo questions like Fla-Flu. I'll add: fla→flamengo-rj... wait \"flamengo\" unambiguous? flamengo rj/pi → ambiguous → \"flamengo-rj\". Yes.\n\nLet me now check Libertadores naming and FIFA Brazilian clubs.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0591e8e57001G8ooE0bKWClm4B","sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","messageID":"msg_0591de5de001hOm6MznVdLe1bX"}}
