sorted(t for t in teams if any(b.lower() in t.lower() for b in big)))\n\nlib = load('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv')\nlibteams = set()\nfor r in lib:\n    libteams.add(r['home_team']); libteams.add(r['away_team'])\nprint(\"\\nLibertadores suffix variants:\")\npat = re.compile(r'-([A-Z]{3})$')\nprint(\" -3letter:\", sorted(t for t in libteams if pat.search(t))[:30])\npat2 = re.compile(r'\\(([A-Z]{2,3})\\)$')\nprint(\" (XX):\", sorted(t for t in libteams if pat2.search(t))[:30])\nprint(\"\\nAll Libertadores teams:\", sorted(libteams))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788201594273,"end":1788201594277}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting — FIFA 19 dataset has these Brazilian clubs: América FC (Minas Gerais), Atlético Mineiro, Atlético Paranaense, Bahia, Botafogo, Ceará Sporting Club, Chapecoense, Cruzeiro, Fluminense, Grêmio, Internacional, Paraná, Santos, Sport Club do Recife, Vitória. Notably NO Flamengo, Palmeiras, Corinthians, São Paulo (they weren't in FIFA 19 due to licensing... actually FIFA 19 does have Brazilian clubs but only some). Let me check \"Flamengo\" in FIFA — it wasn't found by the hint list. So \"Who are the highest-rated players at Flamengo?\" can't be answered from FIFA data — the answer would be \"no Flamengo players in FIFA dataset (licensing)\". That's fine; the tool should return an informative result.\n\nAlso Libertadores uses \"Athletico\" (no suffix!) for Athletico-PR? I see 'Athletico' in the list — that's Athletico Paranaense without any suffix. And \"Atlético-MG\", \"Atlético-PR\", \"América-MG\" with state suffixes. And Corinthians/Flamengo/Grêmio/Palmeiras plain.\n\nNote the important collision: FIFA \"Santos\" is the Brazilian Santos FC (20 players); \"Santos Laguna\" is Mexican. With base \"santos\" ambiguous (sp/ap) → stateless \"santos\" resolves to \"santos-sp\" (most matches). Good.\n\nFIFA \"Vitória\" → \"vitoria\" base, only BA in match data → \"vitoria\". But \"Vitória Guimarães\"/\"Vitória de Setúbal\" are Portuguese — different bases, no collision. Good.\n\nFIFA \"Bahia\" → \"bahia\". \"Paraná\" → \"parana-pr\"? base \"parana\" appears with -PR only in match data → unambiguous → \"parana\". Hmm wait: is there \"Paraná\" state club and also \"Paraná Clube\"? Just \"parana\". OK.\n\nFIFA \"Internacional\" → ambiguous base (rs/sc) → most matches → \"internacional-rs\". Good.\n\nNow the alias table (pre-normalized forms, applied to cleaned base names):\n- \"atletico mineiro\" → atletico/mg\n- \"atletico paranaense\" → atletico/pr\n- \"athletico paranaense\" → atletico/pr\n- \"athletico\" → atletico/pr  (Libertadores naming)\n- \"america fc minas gerais\" → america/mg\n- \"ceara sporting club\" → ceara/ce\n- \"sport club do recife\" → sport/pe\n- \"sport recife\" → sport/pe\n- \"ec bahia\" → bahia/ba\n- \"botafogo rj\" → botafogo/rj? Let me check BR-Football team names — it uses \"Botafogo RJ\"? I saw \"Sport Recife\", \"EC Bahia\", \"Botafogo RJ\" in the sample earlier (\"2014-07-16 Sport Recife Botafogo RJ\"). Need the full list of BR-Football names to build aliases. Let me extract unique names from BR-Football that don't match Brasileirao canonical names and check patterns like \"Botafogo RJ\", \"Palmeiras SP\" (space instead of dash), etc.\n\nAlso Libertadores foreign teams: \"Barcelona-EQU\" → base \"barcelona\", country suffix EQU. And there's \"Barcelona\" (Ecuador) vs FC Barcelona (not in data). For canonicalization of foreign teams: strip 3-letter country suffix → keep base (\"barcelona\"). But wait, \"América de Cali\" etc. — plain. The suffixes in Libertadores: let me check all the suffix patterns. \"Nacional (URU)\", \"The Strongest (BOL)\"? Let me enumerate.\n\nAlso, there's a special case: \"Sport-PE\" vs \"Sport Recife\" vs \"Sport\" — fine. And BR-Football names like \"Palmeiras SP\"? Let me check.\n\nLet me enumerate BR-Football unique team names, and Libertadores suffix patterns.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"p