o-mg (Serie A every season 2003-2022 ~760 matches) vs atletico-pr (~similar!) vs atletico-go... Atletico-MG and Atletico-PR both long Serie A histories — MG slightly more? Doesn't matter much; both are \"correct-ish\" but for FIFA \"Atlético Mineiro\" the alias gives MG explicitly. For FIFA \"Atlético Paranaense\" alias gives PR ✓. Stateless \"atletico\" appears in novo? No — novo has \"Athletico-PR\"/\"Atlético-PR\" with state. OK.\n\nEdge: \"Athletico\" (Libertadores, stateless) — alias → (\"atletico\",\"pr\") ✓.\n\nNow Match dataclass fields: date (datetime.date|None), time (str|None), home_display, away_display, home_key, away_key, home_goals|None, away_goals|None, competition (canonical), season (int|None), round_ (str|None), stage (str|None), venue (str|None), source (filename), plus stats: home_shots, away_shots, home_corners, away_corners, home_attacks, away_attacks, ht_result (home side result WON/DRAW/LOST), source_id (novo ID).\n\nCompetition canonical constants:\n- BRASILEIRAO_A = \"Brasileirão Série A\"\n- BRASILEIRAO_B = \"Brasileirão Série B\"\n- BRASILEIRAO_C = \"Brasileirão Série C\"\n- COPA_DO_BRASIL = \"Copa do Brasil\"\n- LIBERTADORES = \"Copa Libertadores\"\n\nMapping from sources:\n- Brasileirao_Matches.csv → Série A, seasons 2012-2022\n- novo → Série A, 2003-2019 (matches \"Série A\"? The novo dataset is Serie A 2003-2019 — yes, all Serie A. Wait, is it? \"novo_campeonato_brasileiro\" 2003-2019 — Campeonato Brasileiro Série A. 6886/17 ≈ 405/season — Serie A had 380 after 2006; 2003-2005 had 46 rounds (526?)... whatever, it's Série A.)\n- BR-Football: tournament column \"Serie A\"→Série A, \"Serie B\"→Série B, \"Serie C\"→Série C, \"Copa do Brasil\"→Copa do Brasil. NOTE: BR-Football \"Serie A\" 2014-2023 duplicates BM 2014-2022! Primary per season = most matches. BM 380/season vs BR-Football Serie A ~369/season → BM primary ✓. But hmm — one caveat: are BM seasons complete? BM 2012-2022 = 11×380 = 4180 exact ✓ complete. BR-Football Serie A = 368