1 if h=='flamengo' else 0; fw += 1 if a=='flamengo' else 0\n    else: d+=1\nprint(\"\\nFla-Flu BM 2012-2022:\", len(ff), \"matches, flamengo wins:\", fw, \"fluminense wins:\", fl, \"draws:\", d)\n\n# avg goals 2019 Serie A\ng=sum(int(r['home_goal'])+int(r['away_goal']) for r in rows)\nprint(\"avg goals/match 2019 Serie A:\", g/len(rows))\nhw=sum(1 for r in rows if int(r['home_goal'])>int(r['away_goal']))\nprint(\"home win rate 2019:\", hw/len(rows))\n\n# biggest win in BM Serie A\nbest=sorted(rows, key=lambda r: -abs(int(r['home_goal'])-int(r['away_goal'])))[:3]\nprint(\"biggest BM wins:\", [(r['datetime'][:10], r['home_team'], r['home_goal'], r['away_goal'], r['away_team']) for r in best])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788201991690,"end":1788201991693}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The MCPServer API works. `call_tool` is async, returns `CallToolResult` with `.content[0].text`.\n\nNow let me write the full implementation. Plan of files:\n\n1. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/__init__.py` — package docstring, version.\n2. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/models.py` — Match, Player, TeamStats, StandingRow dataclasses.\n3. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py` — team name normalization: cleaning, suffix splitting, alias tables, TeamNameRegistry (two-pass ambiguity resolution + default resolution), fuzzy resolve for user queries.\n4. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/loader.py` — parse all 6 CSVs into Match/Player objects; source registry; primary-source computation; date parsing helpers.\n5. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py` — the query engine (search_matches, head_to_head, team_stats, standings, search_players, statistics, biggest_wins, derbies, find_team, list_teams, list_competitions).\n6. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/formatting.py` — render human-readable answers per the spec's example formats.\n7. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/server.py` — MCPServer with tools wired to engine+formatters; `main()` entry point + `python -m brazilian_soccer_mcp`.\n8. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/__main__.py` — run server.\n9. `tests/` — conftest + BDD GWT test modules + server tests.\n10. `requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml`.\n11. Update `README.md`.\n\nLet me carefully write normalize.py first — the heart of the system.\n\n```python\n# Key concepts:\n# - clean_name(raw): lowercase, strip accents, remove parentheticals, collapse whitespace\n# - split_suffix(cleaned): try alias table for full names; extract trailing state (2-letter BR) or country (3-letter) suffix\n# - registry built from data: base -> {suffix: match_count}\n# - canonical_key(base, suffix): keep suffix in key only when base is ambiguous (registry has >1 distinct suffix)\n# - stateless ambiguous base: default suffix = most-frequent\n```\n\nBrazilian states (27): AC AL AP AM BA CE DF ES GO MA MT MS MG PA PB PR PE PI RJ RN RS RO RR SC SP SE TO.\nCountry codes seen: EQU URU PAR PER VEN. Also possibly ARG BOL CHI COL MEX BRA — strip them too (defensive set).\n\nAlias table (applied on the cleaned full name BEFORE suffix extraction; entries may include the suffix, e.g. \"america fc minas gerais\"):\n\n```python\nFULL_NAME_ALIASES = {\n    \"atletico mineiro\": (\"atletico\", \"mg\"),\n    \"clube atletico mineiro\": (\"atletico\", \"mg\"),\n    \"atletico paranaense\": (\"atletico\", \"pr\"),\n    \"athletico paranaense\": (\"atletico\", \"pr\"),\n    \"athletico\": (\"atletico\", \"pr\"),\n    \"cap\": (\"atletico\", \"pr\"),  # Clube Athletico Paranaense? skip CAP, ambiguous\n    \"america fc minas gerais\": (\"america\", \"mg\"),\n    \"america fc\": (\"america\", \"mg\"),       # FIFA \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" after parenthetical strip\n    \"ceara sporting club\": (\"ceara\", \"ce\"),\n    \"sport club do recife\": (\"sport\", \"pe\"),\n    \"sport recife\": (\"sport\", \"pe\"),\n    \"ec bahia\": (\"bahia\", \"ba\"),\n    \"esporte clube bahia\": (\"bahia\", \"ba\"),\n    \"ec vitoria\": (\"vitoria\", \"ba\"),\n    \"vitoria ec\": (\"vitoria\", \"ba\"),\n    \"esporte clube vitoria\": (\"vitoria\", \"ba\"),\n    \"fortaleza ec\": (\"fortaleza\", \"ce\"),\n    \"fortaleza fc\": (\"fortaleza\", \"ce\"),\n    \"ec internacional\": (\"internacional\", \"sc\"),\n    \"macae esporte fc\": (\"macae esporte\", None),   # hmm \"Macae Esporte FC\" vs \"Macae Esporte RJ\"\n    \"vasco\": (\"vasco da gama\", None),\n    \"cr vasco da gama\": (\"vasco da gama\", None),\n    \"club de regatas vasco da gama\": (\"vasco da gama\", None),\n    \"portuguesa desportos\": (\"portuguesa\", None),\n    \" associacao ...\": skip,\n    \"sao paulo fc\": (\"sao paulo\", None),\n    \"sc corinthians paulista\": (\"corinthians\", None),\n    \"sport club corinthians paulista\": (\"corinthians\", None),\n    \"corinthians\": base corinthians (fine, no alias needed)\n    \"sociedade esportiva palmeiras\": (\"palmeiras\", None),\n    \"se palmeiras\": (\"palmeiras\", None),\n    \"clube de regatas do flamengo\": (\"flamengo\", \"rj\"),\n    \"cr flamengo\": (\"flamengo\", \"rj\"),\n    \"fluminense fc\": (\"fluminense\", \"rj\"),\n    \"gremio fbpa\": (\"gremio\", None),  # Gremio Foot-Ball Porto Alegrense\n    \"gremio foot ball porto alegrense\": (\"gremio\", None),\n    \"sc internacional\": (\"internacional\", \"rs\"),\n    \"sport club internacional\": (\"internacional\", \"rs\"),\n    \"sc gremio\": (\"gremio\", None),\n    \"santos fc\": (\"santos\", \"sp\"),\n    \"peixe\": (\"santos\", \"sp\"),  # nickname — put nicknames separately\n}\n```\n\nWait — careful with \"america fc\": FIFA \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → strip parenthetical → \"america fc\" → alias → (\"america\",\"mg\") ✓. But is there another \"América FC\"? In Mexico \"Club América\" (base \"club america\", different) ✓ fine.\n\nNicknames table (only for user queries, not data):\n```python\nNICKNAMES = {\n    \"fla\": (\"flamengo\", \"rj\"),\n    \"mengao\": (\"flamengo\", \"rj\"),\n    \"flu\": (\"fluminense\", \"rj\"),\n    \"timao\": (\"corinthians\", None),\n    \"verdao\": (\"palmeiras\", None),\n    \"peixe\": (\"santos\", \"sp\"),\n    \"galo\": (\"atletico\", \"mg\"),\n    \"raposa\": (\"cruzeiro\", None),\n    \"furacao\": (\"atletico\", \"pr\"),\n    \"coelho\": (\"botafogo\", \"sp\")?? no — Coelho = Botafogo-SP? Coelho is Botafogo/PB? Actually \"Coelho\" = Botafogo de Ribeirão Preto (SP). Risky, skip.\n    \"leao\": skip,\n    \"tricolor\"? ambiguous skip.\n    \"vovo\": (\"fluminense\", \"rj\")? Tricolor? skip extra.\n    \"nao tem\": skip\n}\n```\n\nSuffix extraction details: cleaned name like \"boavista sport club antigo esporte clube barreira rj\" — wait, clean removes \"(antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\" → \"boavista sport club - rj\" → hmm the dash: \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\" → remove parenthetical → \"Boavista Sport Club - RJ\" → cleaned \"boavista sport club - rj\" → suffix regex `[-\\s]+rj$` → base \"boavista sport club\", state rj ✓. Base registry \"boavista sport club\": only rj → key \"boavista sport club\". And BR-Football \"Boavista RJ\" → base \"boavista\", state rj → key \"boavista\"! Different keys for the same club. Ugh. Small club — accept, or add alias \"boavista sport club\" → \"boavista\"? The alias direction: make both → \"boavista\"? Then cup-data key \"boavista\"... but plain \"Boavista\" stateless... base \"boavista\" registry {rj} single → \"boavista\" ✓. Add alias \"boavista sport club\" → (\"boavista\", None). Also FIFA has \"Boavista FC\" (Portugal) → cleaned \"boavista fc\" → alias? FIFA Boavista FC is Portuguese — do NOT alias to Brazilian Boavista. Leave \"boavista fc\" as its own base → key \"boavista fc\" — distinct from \"boavista\" ✓ correct!\n\nHmm wait, but then match-data \"Boavista RJ\" (base boavista {rj}) vs FIFA \"boavosta fc\" — different keys, correct behavior (different clubs).\n\nOK. Now let me also handle \"bragantino\": registry has sp and pa. Alias (\"bragantino\", sp→\"red bull bragantino\"): rule — aliases can specify state-guard: apply when extracted state is None OR equals the guard. Define BASE_ALIASES: base → (target_base, target_state, allowed_source_states_or_None). Simpler: since alias entries receive the extracted (base, state), implement function `_apply_base_alias(base, state)`:\n- \"bragantino\": if state in (None, \"sp\") → (\"red bull bragantino\", None)\n- \"vasco\": if state is None → (\"vasco da gama\", None)\n- \"novorizontino\": if state in (None, \"sp\") → (\"gremio novorizontino\", None)\n- \"novo hamburgo\"? fine as is.\n- \"metropolitano maringa\"? skip.\n- \"atletico\" stateless? No — that's the ambiguity default, handled separately. But \"athletico\" full-name alias handles Libertadores.\n\nWait \"bragantino\" state None → target \"red bull bragantino\"; but historical novo \"Bragantino\" (2003-2011, stateless in novo) = pre-RB Bragantino SP ✓ correct to merge.\n\nAnd \"red bull brasil\" — separate club (AA Ponte Preta? no, Red Bull Brasil is the extinct farm club). Keep separate ✓.\n\nOne more: \"atletico goianiense\"? BR-Football has \"Atletico GO\"? — \"Atletico-GO\" base atletico state go → atletico-go ✓. Goianiense = same club, if written \"Atlético Goianiense\" → base \"atletico goianiense\" ≠ \"atletico-go\"! Add alias \"atletico goianiense\" → (\"atletico\", \"go\"). Similarly \"atletico sorocaba\"? skip small.\n\nAlso \"parana\" vs \"parana clube\": \"Paraná\" (FIFA, BR-Football \"Parana\"?) base parana {pr} → \"parana\" ✓. If \"Paraná Clube\" appears → alias \"parana clube\" → (\"parana\", None). Add defensively.\n\n\"coritiba\": fine. \"cuiaba\": \"Cuiaba MT\"/\"Cuiabá - MT\" → base cuiaba {mt} single → \"cuiaba\" ✓. But \"Cuiabá EC\"? not in data probably. skip.\n\n\"criciuma\": {sc} → \"criciuma\" ✓. \"chapecoense\" ✓. \"avai\" ✓. \"figueirense\" ✓. \"joinville\" ✓.\n\n\"juventude\" {rs, ma} → juventude-rs / juventude-ma ✓ plain → rs (default most) ✓.\n\n\"nautico\" {pe, rr} ✓. \"santa cruz\" {pe, rn, rs} ✓. \"abc\" {rn} → \"abc\" ✓. \"csa\" ✓. \"crb\" ✓.\n\n\"operario\" {pr, ms, mt} → operario-pr/ms/mt ✓.\n\n\"sao raimundo\" {pa, rr} ✓.\n\n\"rio branco\" {ac, es} ✓.\n\n\"comercial\" {ms, pi} ✓. \"guarani\" {sp, ce} ✓. \"internacional\" {rs, sc} ✓. \"botafogo\" {rj, pb, sp} ✓. \"flamengo\" {rj, pi} ✓. \"fluminense\" {rj, pi} ✓. \"america\" {mg, rn} ✓. \"santos\" {sp, ap} ✓. \"atletico\" {es, pr, go, mg, ba, ac} ✓. \"sport\" {pe} → \"sport\" ✓. \"bahia\" {ba} ✓. \"ceara\" {ce} ✓. \"vitoria\" {ba, es} ✓. \"gremio\" {rs} ✓. \"corinthians\" {sp} ✓. \"palmeiras\" {sp} ✓. \"sao paulo\" {sp} ✓. \"coritiba\" {pr} ✓. \"cruzeiro\" {mg} ✓. \"vasco da gama\" {rj} ✓. \"ponte preta\" {sp} ✓. \"portuguesa\" {sp} ✓. \"goias\" {go} ✓. \"fortaleza\" {ce} ✓. \"cuiaba\" {mt} ✓. \"parana\" {pr} ✓. \"bahia de feira\" {ba} ✓.\n\nForeign: base + country suffix: keep suffix in key iff base appears with >1 distinct suffix OR with a BR state too:\n- \"nacional\": {uru, par, am} → keep → nacional-uru, nacional-par, nacional-am ✓ \n- \"delfin\": {equ} → \"delfin\" ✓\n- \"barcelona\": {equ} → \"barcelona\" ✓\n- \"guarani\": {par, ...} wait — Brazilian \"Guarani-CE\" (Guarany de Sobral is \"guarany de sobral\", different base) and \"Guarani - SP\"... registry guarani {sp, ce?}: from collisions list: \"Guarani - CE\", \"Guarani - SP\", \"Guarani-SP\" → {sp, ce} plus \"Guaraní-PAR\"/\"Guaraní (PAR)\" → par! So guarani {sp, ce, par} → keys guarani-sp, guarani-ce, guarani-par ✓ nice.\n- \"river plate\": {uru} + plain Argentine \"River Plate\" → both → base river plate {uru} single → \"river plate\" (Argentine & Uruguayan collapse — acceptable, documented).\n\nSuffix extraction regex (on cleaned, accent-stripped, lowercased):\n```\nm = re.search(r'(?:^|\\s|[-–])\\s*([a-z]{2})$', name) where group in STATES → strip suffix\nm = re.search(r'(?:^|\\s|[-–])\\s*([a-z]{3})$', name) where group in COUNTRIES → strip, country suffix\n```\nCareful: \"sport boys\" — trailing \"boys\"? Not 2/3-letter. \"ldu\"?? Base itself \"ldu\" — no suffix match (\"ldu\" is whole name, regex requires separator before suffix... \"ldu\" alone: `(?:^|\\s|-)\\s*([a-z]{3})$` would match ^+ldu if ldu in COUNTRIES — it's not. ✓). \"psfc\"? fine. \"goias\" — trailing \"as\"? separator required (space/dash) so \"goias\" won't split ✓. \"ceara\" fine. \"Boa\" (Boa-SC? \"Boa - MG\" base boa {mg} → \"boa\") ✓. \"asa\" ✓ (asa - al → base asa {al} → \"asa\"). \"urt\" ✓. \"pbc\"? fine.\n\nEdge: \"Botafogo PB\" vs \"Botafogo SP\" vs \"Botafogo RJ\" ✓ handled.\n\nEdge: \"ABC - RN\" → base \"abc\" {rn} → \"abc\" ✓.\n\nEdge: \"Athletic Club MG\" → base \"athletic club\" {mg} → \"athletic club\" ✓ (distinct club — Athletic Club (MG) is a real Serie C club ✓).\n\nEdge: BR-Football \"EC Internacional SC\" — trailing \"sc\" → base \"ec internacional\" + state sc → BASE alias \"ec internacional\" → (\"internacional\",\"sc\") ✓.\nBut wait \"EC Vitoria\" → base \"ec vitoria\" (no state suffix — \"vitoria\" not state code... hmm \"EC Vitoria\" cleaned \"ec vitoria\"; trailing 2-letter? \"ia\"? no match ✓) → alias → (\"vitoria\",\"ba\") ✓. \"Vitoria EC\" — trailing \"ec\"?? \"ec\" is NOT a state code ✓ safe. → alias \"vitoria ec\" → (\"vitoria\",\"ba\") ✓. But \"Vitoria ES\" → base vitoria state es → vitoria-es ✓ distinct key (correct — different club from Vitória-BA!).\n\nHmm wait, is that right? \"Vitoria ES\" — Rio Branco-Vitoria? There IS an Esporte Clube Vitória... no, Vitória-ES = \"Doça Mel\"? Whatever the data says — distinct key is correct since it's listed separately.\n\nEdge: \"Fortaleza EC\" trailing \"ec\" not state ✓ → alias → fortaleza. \"Fortaleza FC\" ✓.\nEdge: \"Macae Esporte FC\" vs \"Macae Esporte RJ\": alias \"macae esporte fc\" → (\"macae esporte\", None) ✓ then base \"macae esporte\" {rj} → \"macae esporte\" ✓.\nEdge: \"Central SC\" → base central {sc} → \"central\" ✓.\nEdge: \"Duque De Caxias RJ\" → base \"duque de caxias\" {rj} → ✓.\n\nOK the design handles everything I've seen. Now FIFA clubs like \"Grêmio\" → \"gremio\" ✓, \"Atlético Mineiro\" → full-name alias ✓, \"Santos\" stateless ambiguous → default most-frequent state. Santos-SP vs Santos-AP counts: SP huge ✓ → santos-sp. BUT WAIT: stateless \"Santos\" in LIBERTADORES data (plain \"Santos\" = the Brazilian club ✓ same). And \"Santos Laguna\" base \"santos laguna\" distinct ✓.\n\nStateless defaults computed from data: most frequent suffix per base. For bases where stateless occurrences are the vast majority AND base unambiguous — no suffix anyway.\n\nSubtle: stateless \"Corinthians\" in Libertadores/novo → base corinthians {sp} single → key \"corinthians\" ✓ matches \"Corinthians-SP\" ✓.\n\nNow default resolution when user passes stateless ambiguous name: same rule (most frequent suffix). E.g. user \"Botafogo\" → botafogo-rj ✓. \"America\" → america-mg ✓. \n\nBUT the registry keys use suffixed forms for ambiguous bases — e.g., matches store home_key \"flamengo-rj\". Player club canonicalization: FIFA \"Fluminense\" → \"fluminense-rj\" ✓ matches match data keys ✓. Nice — cross-file queries work (spec: \"Cross-file queries work (e.g., player + match data)\").\n\nHmm, but what about FIFA clubs not in match data at all (e.g., \"Palmeiras\" not in FIFA; \"Paris Saint-Germain\")? Player club keys are computed with the same registry; PSG → \"paris saint germain\" (unregistered base, key = base) ✓ fine.\n\nWait — actually does FIFA have Palmeiras? My club scan didn't show Palmeiras/Flamengo/Corinthians/São Paulo — FIFA 19 didn't include them (they appeared in FIFA 20+... actually FIFA 19 had Brazilian league with Palmeiras? The scan shows it doesn't. Fine.)\n\nRegistry construction: pass 1 over all match files collecting (base→Counter{suffix}) AFTER alias application but WITHOUT ambiguity knowledge (aliases are static). Then pass 2: canonical key per match team = base if registry[base] has 1 suffix else base-suffix. Stateless + ambiguous → default = most_common suffix. \n\nWait, one more subtlety: what about base with suffix where base is UNAMBIGUOUS but a DIFFERENT base exists with longer name? e.g. \"bahia\" {ba} → \"bahia\"; \"bahia de feira\" {ba} → \"bahia de feira\" ✓ distinct keys, correct (different clubs).\n\nAnd stateless base that is unambiguous but the registry ALSO has stateless entries with no suffix recorded: e.g. registry[\"corinthians\"] = {\"sp\": 700, None: 50}? Hmm — do I track None-suffix occurrences? If base unambiguous (all sp or None) → key \"corinthians\" regardless ✓. For ambiguous bases with None occurrences: \"flamengo\" {\"rj\": 600, \"pi\": 2, None: 40}?? Where would stateless \"Flamengo\" (Libertadores) go? → default most-common = rj → key flamengo-rj ✓. So registry counts None under the default at key-computation time. I'll store Counter with None keys and treat None as \"resolve to most common non-None suffix\".\n\nPlayer \"Club\" field: apply same canonicalization. FIFA \"Botafogo\" stateless → default → botafogo-rj ✓ (FIFA Botafogo is the RJ one ✓ correct!).\n\nNow write the code. Also formatting module per spec answer formats. Let me write all files now.\n\n**models.py**:\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True) Match: ...\n@dataclass(frozen=True) Player: ...\n@dataclass StandingRow: ...\n@dataclass TeamStats: ...\n```\n\nKeep dataclasses light (slots for perf). 20k+ matches? Total: 4180+1337+1255+10296+6886 = 23,954 matches. Fine.\n\n**loader.py**: parse each file. Date parsing:\n- \"2012-05-19 18:30:00\" → date(2012,5,19), time \"18:30\"\n- \"2023-09-24\" → date\n- \"29/03/2003\" → date\n- \"NA\" → None\nGoals parse: int(float(x)) if not in {NA, -, ''}.\n\nSource files constant → source label: \"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\" etc.\n\nPrimary source per (competition, season): counts; priority = [BM, CUP, NOVO, LIB, BRF]; primary = highest-priority source with count ≥ 0.9 × max_count... wait actually let me reconsider: for Série A 2012-2019 both BM and novo have exactly 380 → BM higher priority → BM primary ✓. For Série A 2014-2022: BM 380, BRF ~369 → BM primary ✓ (BM priority anyway). Série A 2023: BRF only ✓. Série A 2003-2011: novo only ✓. Copa do Brasil 2014-2020: CUP > BRF counts → CUP primary ✓. 2021: CUP 108, BRF 111 → 0.9×111 = 99.9 ≤ 108 ✓ CUP primary (higher priority) ✓. 2022-2023 BRF ✓. \n\nThe 0.9 rule only matters when high-priority source has significantly fewer matches. Good.\n\nAlso dedupe within primary? If primary source has duplicate rows (same date+teams)... unlikely; skip.\n\n**Engine queries** — signatures designed above. Filters: team resolution via normalizer; raise TeamNotFound error with suggestions; competition resolution via alias table returning list of canonical competition names.\n\nStage/round filters: for Libertadores stage ∈ {group stage, round of 16, quarterfinals, semifinals, final}; for Copa do Brasil round 1-8 with 8=final, 7=semifinal (label mapping); \"finals\" special: stage==\"final\" OR (competition Copa do Brasil AND round==\"8\"). I'll implement stage parameter accepting: \"final\", \"semifinal\", \"quarterfinal\", \"round of 16\", \"group\" etc. mapping to each competition's representation:\n- Libertadores: final/semifinals/quarterfinals/round of 16/group stage ✓ direct\n- Copa do Brasil: final→round 8, semifinal→round 7, quarterfinal→round 6? Let me check cup rounds: 2019: round5:16, round6:8, round7:4, round8:2. Round-of-16 = round 5 (16 matches) ✓, quarterfinal = round 6 (8) ✓, semifinal = round 7 (4) ✓, final = round 8 (2) ✓. But earlier rounds vary by season (preliminaries). So mapping: final=8, semi=7, quarter=6, r16=5. For older seasons (2012: rounds 1-6, 6=2 matches → final=6!). Hmm: 2012 rounds: 1:53, 2:29, 3:16, 4:8, 5:4, 6:2 → final = LAST round of that season (max round with ≤2 matches). Robust approach for \"final\": round == max round in that season AND match count ≤ 2. I'll compute per season: final_round = max(round for season). For 2019 max=8 ✓ final. 2012 max=6 ✓ final. \n\nSo stage filter \"final\": for Libertadores stage==\"final\"; for Copa do Brasil: round == max_round(season); for others: no stage info → return matches noting unavailable? Série A has no final. OK.\n\n**Standings**: compute from primary matches of competition+season with non-None goals. Rows sorted by pts, wins, GD, GF. Include: position, team display, P, W, D, L, GF, GA, GD, Pts. Champion = row 1 when season \"complete enough\" (played == expected where expected = 380 for 20-team double round robin... general: total played matches == len(teams)*(len(teams)-1)). For incomplete: mark \"(incomplete season in data: X/Y matches)\". Relegated = bottom 4 when 20 teams. Team display name: pick most common display variant for the key (I'll track display-name counts per key).\n\nAlso \"Top scorers (if inferable from data)\" — NOT inferable (no scorer data) → I'll note that in competition_info: \"Top scorers not available in provided datasets (no per-goal scorer data)\". Honest.\n\n**statistics(competition=None, season=None)**: over filtered matches with results: count, avg goals/match, home win %, draw %, away win %, avg home goals, avg away goals, biggest win. \n\n**biggest_wins**: sort by margin desc, then total goals desc; limit.\n\n**team_stats**: filters + venue home/away/all. Output TeamStats(matches, wins, draws, losses, gf, ga, win_rate...). Also recent form? skip.\n\n**head_to_head**: all matches between keys (either order), aggregate wins per team + draws, list recent matches. Note spec format includes derby name when applicable: \"Flamengo vs Fluminense (Fla-Flu derby)\". I'll look up derby table by key pair and add name.\n\n**derbies**: curated DERBY list: name, teams (canonical keys), competition filter optional. Query: derby name optional + season/competition filters → matches between pair. Default: all derbies with counts.\n\n**find_team**: resolve + variants (display names seen), match count, first/last appearance, competitions played.\n\n**search_players**: filters name substring (case/accent-insensitive!), nationality exact-ish (case-insensitive; \"Brazil\" or \"Brazilian\" → Brazil), club → canonical resolve (fuzzy too: club \"Flamengo\" → key), position (exact FIFA code or group: GK, DF→{LB,CB,RB,LWB,RWB,SW}, MF→{CDM,CM,CAM,LM,RM}, FW→{ST,CF,LW,RW,LF,RF}), min_overall, order_by (overall|potential|age|name), limit. Name matching accent-insensitive: \"Gabriel Barbosa\" → normalize both sides. If no results and name given → difflib suggestions.\n\n**club report** (for \"Which players play for Flamengo?\"): search_players(club=...) formatted.\n\n**Competition info**: per competition: seasons available, sources, matches per season, teams count. list_competitions() with aliases.\n\n**Formatting**: functions returning strings per spec formats. E.g. format_match_list(header, matches, total), format_h2h, format_team_stats, format_standings, format_player_list, format_stats, format_biggest_wins. The spec formats use competition display names like \"Brasileirão Round 22\" — I'll do \"(Brasileirão Série A, Round 22)\" or for Libertadores \"(Libertadores, Final)\".\n\n**server.py**: MCPServer with ~12 tools, each calling engine + formatter. Data dir resolution: env var BRAZILIAN_SOCCER_DATA_DIR or default `data/kaggle` relative to package parent? Server should work from repo root. Default: search upward from CWD for data/kaggle, else relative to package file (../../data/kaggle). Implement `find_data_dir()`.\n\nEngine caching: module-level singleton via `get_engine()`.\n\n**Performance**: load time ~1-2s (fifa 9MB csv with csv.DictReader ~18k×100 cells — fine).\n\n**Tests** (BDD GWT): I'll structure each test with Gherkin docstring:\n\n```python\ndef test_...():\n    \"\"\"\n    Feature: Match Queries\n    Scenario: Find matches between two teams\n      Given the match data is loaded\n      When I search for matches between \"Flamengo\" and \"Fluminense\"\n      Then I should receive a list of matches\n      And each match should have date, scores, and competition\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\nAnd use a GWT-flavored assertion flow with given/when/then helper comments. Keep tests meaningful with real data assertions:\n\n- test_normalize: atletico variants collide to one key; botafogo 3-way; vasco; athletico libertadores; FIFA atlético mineiro; accents; suffix strip; nicknames; find_team fuzzy.\n- test_matches: fla-flu search returns matches w/ date+score+competition; both directions; competition filter; season filter; date range; 2019 libertadores final content; copa do brasil finals via stage=final (Santos-Palmeiras 2015 present); unplayed matches have None goals and excluded from stats.\n- test_team: palmeiras 2023 stats — 2023 Série A from BRF: Palmeiras... compute at runtime? Better: assert structure + internal consistency (matches == W+D+L, GF/GA) + spot-check vs known: Corinthians home record 2022 — compute expected by independent pandas-free python in test? That duplicates loader logic. Instead assert W+D+L=matches and positive counts, plus a couple of hard facts I can verify now with a quick script (e.g., Palmeiras 2022 Serie A: 23W 12D 3L? Real world: Palmeiras 2022 = 23W 12D 3L 81 pts champion ✓ — I'll verify from data before writing the assertion).\n- test_players: 827 Brazilians; Neymar 92 top; Fluminense 20 players; positions filter FW at Santos; club resolution via canonical keys (players at \"fluminense\" match team query); Gabriel Barbosa → not found → suggestions include \"Gabriel Jesus\" (verify).\n- test_competition: standings 2019 → Flamengo 1st with 90 pts (matches spec!); 20 teams; relegated 2019 (last 4: none of the famous... 2019 relegated: CSA, Chapecoense, Cruzeiro, Fortaleza? wait Fortaleza stayed... 2019 relegated were CSA, Chapecoense, Cruzeiro, Fortaleza?? No — 2019 Série A relegated: CSA, Chapecoense, Cruzeiro, Fortaleza? Hmm, Fortaleza finished 9th. Relegated 2019: CSA (20th), Chapecoense (19th), Cruzeiro (17th)... 4 relegated: CSA, Chapecoense, Cruzeiro, Fortaleza is wrong — it was CSA, Chapecoense, Cruzeiro, and Fortaleza?? No! Avaí! 2019 relegated: Avaí, CSA, Chapecoense, Cruzeiro. ✓ I'll compute from data and just assert count==4 and champion).\n  Also standings completeness: 380 played for 2019; teams=20.\n- test_statistics: avg goals ~2.x; home win rate; biggest wins include 2019 Flamengo 5-0? compute top margin dynamically and assert ordering; biggest win margin ≥ some value; 2003 round format.\n- test_h2h: fla-flu aggregate counts = sum of matches; derby name shown.\n- test_server: list tools (≥12); call search_matches tool returns text containing \"Flamengo\"; call standings tool for 2019 contains \"Flamengo\" and \"90\"; call find_team.\n- test_performance (marked): engine load < 10s (cold), search < 2s, standings < 5s.\n\nconftest.py: session-scoped engine fixture (loads once).\n\nAlso a `pytest.ini`/pyproject config with testpaths.\n\nTime to verify a few hard facts from the data to embed in tests (Palmeiras 2022, Corinthians home 2022, fla-flu counts, avg goals 2019). Let me compute using my planned logic mentally via quick script (independent mini-implementation to avoid circularity).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05924fda300110kN70dXpaJFln","sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","messageID":"msg_05922d90300123S6cmQ9ZPXSzH"}}
