{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788202035310,"sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_153cab141af9489288abd514","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, re, unicodedata\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef sa(s): return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFD', s) if unicodedata.category(c)!='Mn')\ndef canon(n):\n    n = sa(n).lower().strip()\n    n = re.sub(r'\\s*\\(antigo[^)]*\\)', '', n)\n    m = re.search(r'^(.*?)[\\s\\-]+(sp|rj|mg|pr|rs|sc|pe|ba|ce|go|mt|ms|pa|pb|rn|al|se|pi|ma|to|ro|rr|ac|ap|am|df|es)$', n)\n    if m and m.group(1).strip(): return (m.group(1).strip(), m.group(2))\n    return (n, None)\n\ndef load(path):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nbrf = load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\na22 = [r for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'][:4]=='2022']\nprint(\"BRF 2022 Serie A matches:\", len(a22))\nbm = load('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nb22 = [r for r in bm if r['season']=='2022' and r['home_goal'] not in ('NA','')]\nprint(\"BM 2022 played:\", len(b22))\n\n# Palmeiras 2022 from BRF\ndef rec(rows, base, season_key, date_prefix=None):\n    w=d=l=gf=ga=n=0\n    for r in rows:\n        h,_ = canon(r['home']); a,_ = canon(r['away'])\n        hg,ag = int(float(r['home_goal'])), int(float(r['away_goal']))\n        if base in (h,a):\n            n+=1\n            if h==base: sc,oc=gf_,ga_=hg,ag\n            else: sc,oc=ag,hg\n            gf+=sc; ga+=oc\n            if sc>oc: w+=1\n            elif sc==oc: d+=1\n            else: l+=1\n    return n,w,d,l,gf,ga\nprint(\"Palmeiras 2022 BRF:\", rec(a22, 'palmeiras', None))\nch22=[r for r in a22 if canon(r['home'])[0]=='corinthians']\nprint(\"Corinthians home 2022 BRF:\", rec(ch22, 'corinthians', None))\n\n# 2022 standings BRF top2 + bottom4\ndef table(rows):\n    t={}\n    for r in rows:\n        h,_=canon(r['home']); a,_=canon(r['away'])\n        hg,ag=int(float(r['home_goal'])),int(float(r['away_goal']))\n        for x in (h,a): t.setdefault(x,{'p':0,'w':0,'d':0,'l':0,'gf':0,'ga':0})\n        if hg>ag: t[h]['p']+=3;t[h]['w']+=1;t[a]['l']+=1\n        elif hg<ag: t[a]['p']+=3;t[a]['w']+=1;t[h]['l']+=1\n        else: t[h]['p']+=1;t[a]['p']+=1;t[h]['d']+=1;t[a]['d']+=1\n        t[h]['gf']+=hg;t[h]['ga']+=ag;t[a]['gf']+=ag;t[a]['ga']+=hg\n    return sorted(t.items(), key=lambda kv:(-kv[1]['p'],-kv[1]['w'],-(kv[1]['gf']-kv[1]['ga'])))\nst22 = table(a22)\nprint(\"2022 BRF top2:\", [(t,e['p']) for t,e in st22[:2]], \" bottom4:\", [(t,e['p']) for t,e in st22[-4:]], \" teams:\", len(st22))\n\n# Full-dataset Fla-Flu with stateful keys (BM primary 2012-2022, novo 2003-2011, BRF 2023, all comps)\nnv = load('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nlib = load('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv')\ncup = load('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv')\nallm = []\nfor r in bm:\n    if r['season']>='2012': allm.append((r['datetime'][:10], canon(r['home_team'])[0]+'/'+canon(r['home_team'])[1], canon(r['away_team'])[0]+'/'+canon(r['away_team'])[1], r['home_goal'], r['away_goal'], 'brasileirao', r['season']))\nfor r in nv:\n    if r['Ano']<'2012': allm.append((r['Data'][6:]+'-'+r['Data'][3:5]+'-'+r['Data'][:2], canon(r['Equipe_mandante'])[0], canon(r['Equipe_visitante'])[0], r['Gols_mandante'], r['Gols_visitante'], 'brasileirao', r['Ano']))\nfor r in a22pass := [r for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'][:4]=='2023']:\n    pass\nfor r in [r for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'][:4]=='2023']:\n    allm.append((r['date'], canon(r['home'])[0], canon(r['away'])[0], str(int(float(r['home_goal']))), str(int(float(r['away_goal']))), 'brasileirao', '2023'))\ndef is_ff(h,a): return (h=='flamengo/rj' and a=='fluminense/rj') or (h=='fluminense/rj' and a=='flamengo/rj') or (h=='flamengo' and a=='fluminense') or (h=='fluminense' and a=='flamengo')\nff=[m for m in allm if is_ff(m[1],m[2]) and m[3] not in ('NA','','-')]\nfw=fld=d=0\nfor m in ff:\n    h,a,hg,ag=m[1],m[2],int(m[3]),int(m[4])\n    if hg>ag: fw += 1 if 'flamengo' in h else 0; fld += 1 if 'flamengo' in a else 0\n    elif hg<ag: fld += 1 if 'flamengo' in h else 0; fw += 1 if 'flamengo' in a else 0\n    else: d+=1\nprint(\"\\nFla-Flu Brasileirao 2003-2023:\", len(ff), \"matches | Flamengo:\", fw, \"Fluminense:\", fld, \"Draws:\", d)\nEOF","workdir":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5"},"output":"  File \"<stdin>\", line 66\n    for r in a22pass := [r for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'][:4]=='2023']:\n                     ^^\nSyntaxError: invalid syntax\n","metadata":{"output":"  File \"<stdin>\", line 66\n    for r in a22pass := [r for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'][:4]=='2023']:\n                     ^^\nSyntaxError: invalid syntax\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, re, unicodedata\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef sa(s): return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFD', s) if unicodedata.category(c)!='Mn')\ndef canon(n):\n    n = sa(n).lower().strip()\n    n = re.sub(r'\\s*\\(antigo[^)]*\\)', '', n)\n    m = re.search(r'^(.*?)[\\s\\-]+(sp|rj|mg|pr|rs|sc|pe|ba|ce|go|mt|ms|pa|pb|rn|al|se|pi|ma|to|ro|rr|ac|ap|am|df|es)$', n)\n    if m and m.group(1).strip(): return (m.group(1).strip(), m.group(2))\n    return (n, None)\n\ndef load(path):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nbrf = load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\na22 = [r for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'][:4]=='2022']\nprint(\"BRF 2022 Serie A matches:\", len(a22))\nbm = load('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nb22 = [r for r in bm if r['season']=='2022' and r['home_goal'] not in ('NA','')]\nprint(\"BM 2022 played:\", len(b22))\n\n# Palmeiras 2022 from BRF\ndef rec(rows, base, season_key, date_prefix=None):\n    w=d=l=gf=ga=n=0\n    for r in rows:\n        h,_ = canon(r['home']); a,_ = canon(r['away'])\n        hg,ag = int(float(r['home_goal'])), int(float(r['away_goal']))\n        if base in (h,a):\n            n+=1\n            if h==base: sc,oc=gf_,ga_=hg,ag\n            else: sc,oc=ag,hg\n            gf+=sc; ga+=oc\n            if sc>oc: w+=1\n            elif sc==oc: d+=1\n            else: l+=1\n    return n,w,d,l,gf,ga\nprint(\"Palmeiras 2022 BRF:\", rec(a22, 'palmeiras', None))\nch22=[r for r in a22 if canon(r['home'])[0]=='corinthians']\nprint(\"Corinthians home 2022 BRF:\", rec(ch22, 'corinthians', None))\n\n# 2022 standings BRF top2 + bottom4\ndef table(rows):\n    t={}\n    for r in rows:\n        h,_=canon(r['home']); a,_=canon(r['away'])\n        hg,ag=int(float(r['home_goal'])),int(float(r['away_goal']))\n        for x in (h,a): t.setdefault(x,{'p':0,'w':0,'d':0,'l':0,'gf':0,'ga':0})\n        if hg>ag: t[h]['p']+=3;t[h]['w']+=1;t[a]['l']+=1\n        elif hg<ag: t[a]['p']+=3;t[a]['w']+=1;t[h]['l']+=1\n        else: t[h]['p']+=1;t[a]['p']+=1;t[h]['d']+=1;t[a]['d']+=1\n        t[h]['gf']+=hg;t[h]['ga']+=ag;t[a]['gf']+=ag;t[a]['ga']+=hg\n    return sorted(t.items(), key=lambda kv:(-kv[1]['p'],-kv[1]['w'],-(kv[1]['gf']-kv[1]['ga'])))\nst22 = table(a22)\nprint(\"2022 BRF top2:\", [(t,e['p']) for t,e in st22[:2]], \" bottom4:\", [(t,e['p']) for t,e in st22[-4:]], \" teams:\", len(st22))\n\n# Full-dataset Fla-Flu with stateful keys (BM primary 2012-2022, novo 2003-2011, BRF 2023, all comps)\nnv = load('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nlib = load('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv')\ncup = load('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv')\nallm = []\nfor r in bm:\n    if r['season']>='2012': allm.append((r['datetime'][:10], canon(r['home_team'])[0]+'/'+canon(r['home_team'])[1], canon(r['away_team'])[0]+'/'+canon(r['away_team'])[1], r['home_goal'], r['away_goal'], 'brasileirao', r['season']))\nfor r in nv:\n    if r['Ano']<'2012': allm.append((r['Data'][6:]+'-'+r['Data'][3:5]+'-'+r['Data'][:2], canon(r['Equipe_mandante'])[0], canon(r['Equipe_visitante'])[0], r['Gols_mandante'], r['Gols_visitante'], 'brasileirao', r['Ano']))\nfor r in a22pass := [r for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'][:4]=='2023']:\n    pass\nfor r in [r for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'][:4]=='2023']:\n    allm.append((r['date'], canon(r['home'])[0], canon(r['away'])[0], str(int(float(r['home_goal']))), str(int(float(r['away_goal']))), 'brasileirao', '2023'))\ndef is_ff(h,a): return (h=='flamengo/rj' and a=='fluminense/rj') or (h=='fluminense/rj' and a=='flamengo/rj') or (h=='flamengo' and a=='fluminense') or (h=='fluminense' and a=='flamengo')\nff=[m for m in allm if is_ff(m[1],m[2]) and m[3] not in ('NA','','-')]\nfw=fld=d=0\nfor m in ff:\n    h,a,hg,ag=m[1],m[2],int(m[3]),int(m[4])\n    if hg>ag: fw += 1 if 'flamengo' in h else 0; fld += 1 if 'flamengo' in a else 0\n    elif hg<ag: fld += 1 if 'flamengo' in h else 0; fw += 1 if 'flamengo' in a else 0\n    else: d+=1\nprint(\"\\nFla-Flu Brasileirao 2003-2023:\", len(ff), \"matches | Flamengo:\", fw, \"Fluminense:\", fld, \"Draws:\", d)\nEOF","time":{"start":1788202035305,"end":1788202035308}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Two issues found in my quick verification script:\n\n1. **2019 standings shows 19 teams with \"atletico\" at 112 points!** — My quick script's `canon` strips state suffix, so \"Atletico-MG\" and \"Atletico-PR\" BOTH collapsed to \"atletico\" (2 teams' matches merged = ~76 matches, 112 pts). This CONFIRMS the need to keep the state for ambiguous bases (my registry design handles exactly this). With my real normalizer, atletico-mg and atletico-pr stay separate and the table will have 20 teams. Good validation of the design!\n\n2. Corinthians home 2022 = 15 matches?? Should be 19. My filter `rec([r for r in bm if home=='corinthians'],'corinthians','2022')` — inside rec I check `r['season']!=season` — fine... 15 matches with goals? 2022 has NA goals for 82 matches! Some Corinthians home 2022 matches unplayed (dataset exported mid... no wait, BM has all 380 rows for 2022 but 82 with NA goals — those are postponed rescheduled games that were never backfilled). So Corinthians 2022 home = 19 total, 15 played at export. Real 2022 Corinthians home record: 19 matches. The data shows 15 played. My earlier claim \"BM seasons complete\" was wrong — rows exist but some unplayed. For tests, assert from the data (15 played home matches for Corinthians in 2022 — but if primary source logic picks BRF for 2022 (BRF Serie A 2022 = 369 matches with goals) — hmm! 2022: BM has 380 rows but 298 played; BRF has ~369 played. Primary source = highest priority with count ≥ 0.9 × max. BM count 298 (or 380?). Do I count rows or played matches? If I count ROWS: BM 380 ≥ 0.9×369 → BM primary. If played: BM 298 < 0.9×369=332 → BRF primary!\n\nWhich is better? For \"who won 2022\" the BRF data (more played matches) gives a more complete table. 2022 champion = Palmeiras. With BM primary (298 played), standings would still show Palmeiras top (they were runaway leaders). Let me count played matches per source for 2022 Série A: BM played = 4180 total NA 82 → but which seasons? The NA rows: 2016 (Chapecoense round 38) + 2022 several. Let me compute: 2022 BM rows with goals. And BRF 2022 Serie A count. Then decide: primary = argmax(played matches), tie→priority, plus 0.9 rule? Simplest: primary = source with most PLAYED matches; tie → priority. For 2012-2019 Série A: BM 380 played = novo 380 → tie → BM (priority) ✓. 2014-2022: BM 380 or 298 vs BRF ~369: 2014-2021 BM 380 > BRF ✓; 2022 BM 298 vs BRF ? — need the number. If BRF 2022 = 369 → BRF primary for 2022. Then Palmeiras 2022 record from BRF: let me compute (using BRF team names: \"Palmeiras\"). Also Corinthians home 2022 would come from BRF.\n\nHmm, wait — but BRF names lack states: \"Sao Paulo\", \"Palmeiras\" — my normalizer handles ✓.\n\nLet me get BRF 2022 Serie A stats: Palmeiras full record and Corinthians home record. Also confirm 2022 champion = Palmeiras in BRF data.\n\n3. Fla-Flu BM 2012-2022: 22 matches, 9-9-4 ✓ (plus 2023+ from BRF? 2023 Fla-Flu in BRF Serie A: yes 2 more). Spec example says \"12 wins, 8 wins, 7 draws\" — illustrative only; whatever the full dataset gives is the answer. Let me compute the full-dataset H2H (BM primary 2012-2022 + novo 2003-2011 + BRF 2023 + Libertadores + Copa do Brasil where both teams meet).\n\nNote my quick canon also collapsed \"Goias-GO\"→\"goias\" fine.\n\nAlso interesting: biggest BM wins are 6-1 (not 8-0; the 8-0 Santos-Bolivar in the spec example isn't in our data — spec examples are illustrative). But BR-Football dataset might have bigger margins. Fine.\n\nNow — 2019 champion Flamengo 90 pts 28W 6D 4L matches the spec example EXACTLY (spec: \"1. Flamengo - 90 pts (28W, 6D, 4L) - Champion; 2. Santos - 74 pts (22W, 8D, 8L); 3. Palmeiras - 74 pts (21W, 11D, 6L)\") — my computation gives Santos 74 (22W 8D 8L) ✓ and third should be Palmeiras 74 (21W 11D 6L) — my collapsed-atletico bug aside, let me verify Palmeiras is 3rd with 74 when atletico is split properly. Atletico-PR 2019: 15th? Palmeiras 3rd ✓ real world. Great test assertion: 2019 top-3 exactly as spec.\n\nBottom 4 2019 (relegated): real world = CSA, Chapecoense, Cruzeiro, Avaí ✓ my computation (with avai at 20 pts) ✓✓.\n\nLet me now fix my verification to use proper stateful keys and check 2022 BRF numbers + Palmeiras 2022 + full-dataset Fla-Flu.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05925a82c001i6VLktAZ5zllSg","sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","messageID":"msg_05924ff79001kh5o5ZxGf4VDJ9"}}
