{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788202328567,"sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_4c9526027aba4d0ba825eb84","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","oldString":"def clean_name(raw: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Lowercase, de-accent and lightly punctuate a team name.\"\"\"\n    name = strip_accents(str(raw)).lower()\n    name = re.sub(r\"\\(antigo[^)]*\\)\", \" \", name)\n    name = name.replace(\"'\", \"\").replace(\".\", \" \")\n    name = re.sub(r\"[\\s\\-]+\", \" \", name).strip()\n    return name","newString":"def clean_name(raw: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Lowercase, de-accent and lightly punctuate a team name.\n\n    Parenthetical qualifiers containing spaces (e.g. \"(antigo Esporte Clube\n    Barreira)\", \"(Minas Gerais)\") are dropped; short country qualifiers such\n    as \"(URU)\" are kept for suffix detection.\n    \"\"\"\n    name = strip_accents(str(raw)).lower()\n    name = re.sub(r\"\\s*\\([^)]*\\s[^)]*\\)\", \" \", name)\n    name = name.replace(\"'\", \"\").replace(\".\", \" \")\n    name = re.sub(r\"[\\s\\-]+\", \" \", name).strip()\n    return name"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -113,11 +113,16 @@\n     )\n \n \n def clean_name(raw: str) -> str:\n-    \"\"\"Lowercase, de-accent and lightly punctuate a team name.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Lowercase, de-accent and lightly punctuate a team name.\n+\n+    Parenthetical qualifiers containing spaces (e.g. \"(antigo Esporte Clube\n+    Barreira)\", \"(Minas Gerais)\") are dropped; short country qualifiers such\n+    as \"(URU)\" are kept for suffix detection.\n+    \"\"\"\n     name = strip_accents(str(raw)).lower()\n-    name = re.sub(r\"\\(antigo[^)]*\\)\", \" \", name)\n+    name = re.sub(r\"\\s*\\([^)]*\\s[^)]*\\)\", \" \", name)\n     name = name.replace(\"'\", \"\").replace(\".\", \" \")\n     name = re.sub(r\"[\\s\\-]+\", \" \", name).strip()\n     return name\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -113,11 +113,16 @@\n     )\n \n \n def clean_name(raw: str) -> str:\n-    \"\"\"Lowercase, de-accent and lightly punctuate a team name.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Lowercase, de-accent and lightly punctuate a team name.\n+\n+    Parenthetical qualifiers containing spaces (e.g. \"(antigo Esporte Clube\n+    Barreira)\", \"(Minas Gerais)\") are dropped; short country qualifiers such\n+    as \"(URU)\" are kept for suffix detection.\n+    \"\"\"\n     name = strip_accents(str(raw)).lower()\n-    name = re.sub(r\"\\(antigo[^)]*\\)\", \" \", name)\n+    name = re.sub(r\"\\s*\\([^)]*\\s[^)]*\\)\", \" \", name)\n     name = name.replace(\"'\", \"\").replace(\".\", \" \")\n     name = re.sub(r\"[\\s\\-]+\", \" \", name).strip()\n     return name\n \n","additions":7,"deletions":2},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788202328562,"end":1788202328565}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait, there's a bug in `variants()`: \n\n```python\ndef variants(self, key: str) -> list[str]:\n    base = key.rsplit(\"-\", 1)[0] if key not in self._suffix_counts else key\n```\nThe logic is inverted/confusing. For key \"flamengo-rj\", base = \"flamengo\" ✓. For key \"corinthians\" (in suffix_counts) → base = \"corinthians\" ✓. For key \"atletico-mg\" → rsplit gives \"atletico\" ✓. But for a key like \"botafogo rj\"... keys use \"-\" only when ambiguous. Hmm, what about key \"gremio novorizontino\" (contains space, no dash) → rsplit(\"-\",1)[0] = whole key ✓ fine. And \"vasco da gama\" ✓. Edge: base names that themselves contain a dash? None after cleaning (dashes became spaces in clean_name; keys built from base + \"-\" + suffix). OK the logic works but is convoluted. Let me simplify: base = key if key in self._suffix_counts else key.rsplit(\"-\", 1)[0]. Actually current code: `key.rsplit(\"-\", 1)[0] if key not in self._suffix_counts else key` — if key IS a base (in suffix_counts) → use key as base ✓; else split off suffix ✓. That's right, just awkwardly written. Fine, leave.\n\nAnother issue: `canonical_key(context=\"players\")` — I apply TEAM_ALIASES/Base aliases for players context, but the full-name lookup at the top of `_decompose` already handles TEAM_ALIASES for any context ✓. The players-context block re-checks `base in TEAM_ALIASES` for bases like \"atletico mineiro\" — but those would already match in `_decompose` step 1 (cleaned in TEAM_ALIASES). Wait — `_decompose` checks `cleaned in TEAM_ALIASES` BEFORE suffix split: \"atletico mineiro\" (no suffix) → TEAM_ALIASES ✓ hit. But \"atlético mineiro - mg\"? → cleaned \"atletico mineiro - mg\" not in aliases → suffix split → base \"atletico mineiro\", state \"mg\" → context matches → _strip_ec_fc no-op → BASE_ALIASES no → returns (\"atletico mineiro\", \"mg\") → key would be \"atletico mineiro-mg\"?? Not seen in data, so _suffix_counts empty → key = base = \"atletico mineiro\" → wrong-ish but this exact string doesn't occur. For players context: \"Atlético Mineiro\" → cleaned \"atletico mineiro\" → TEAM_ALIASES hit in _decompose ✓. OK.\n\nBut the players-context block in `canonical_key` handles the case where base (after suffix split) is in TEAM_ALIASES — e.g., FIFA \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → cleaned \"america fc minas gerais\" — wait clean_name removes parentheticals ONLY for \"(antigo...)\". \"(Minas Gerais)\" stays! cleaned = \"america fc (minas gerais)\". Hmm! Then TEAM_ALIASES lookup fails (\"america fc (minas gerais)\" not in table), suffix split: _COUNTRY_PAREN_RE matches? \"(minas gerais)\" is 2+ letters... pattern `\\((?P<country>[a-z]{2,3})\\)$` requires 2-3 letters only — \"minas gerais\" has a space, no match ✓. _STATE_SUFFIX_RE: trailing \"(minas gerais)\" — \"[a-z]{2}$\"? The regex needs the final token to be 2-letter state — \"gerais\" is 6 chars, no ✓. So base = \"america fc (minas gerais)\" — ugh.\n\nFix: clean_name should strip ALL parentheticals, not just \"(antigo ...)\": \"(URU)\" handled by _COUNTRY_PAREN_RE on the cleaned name — if clean_name strips all parentheticals, \"Nacional (URU)\" → \"nacional\" and country info is LOST (would collide Nacional-URU vs Nacional-PAR!). Hmm.\n\nBetter: clean_name strips parentheticals ONLY when they contain spaces (multi-word parentheticals like \"(antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\", \"(Minas Gerais)\") and keeps short ones \"(URU)\", \"(PAR)\". Then:\n- \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\" → \"boavista sport club - rj\" → suffix → base \"boavista sport club\" ✓\n- \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → \"america fc\" → TEAM_ALIASES → (\"america\",\"mg\") ✓\n- \"Nacional (URU)\" → \"nacional (uru)\" → _COUNTRY_PAREN_RE → base \"nacional\", country \"uru\" ✓\n\nImplement: `re.sub(r\"\\s*\\([^)]*\\s[^)]*\\)\", \" \", name)` — removes parentheticals containing whitespace. ✓\n\nAlso for the \"players\" context, the systematic EC/FC strip is skipped ✓ (protects \"Boavista FC\" Portugal). But \"Fortaleza FC\"?? — that's a MATCH-data name (BRF) ✓ matches context strips it. FIFA has no \"Fortaleza FC\". ✓\n\nOne more subtle bug: `_decompose` for context \"matches\": after suffix split, if stripped base is in TEAM_ALIASES I apply the alias but IGNORE the extracted state. E.g., \"Atletico Mineiro - MG\" (hypothetical) → suffix split → base \"atletico mineiro\" state \"mg\" → alias → (\"atletico\",\"mg\") — state matches anyway ✓. But \"Sport Club do Recife - PE\"? → base \"sport club do recife\", state pe → alias (\"sport\",\"pe\") ✓ consistent. Fine.\n\nAlso `resolve()`: cleaned query \"sport club corinthians paulista\" → TEAM_ALIASES ✓ → (\"corinthians\", None) → key \"corinthians\" ✓. Query \"corinthians sp\" → suffix split → base \"corinthians\", state \"sp\" → key \"corinthians\" (unambiguous base) ✓. Query \"atletico\" → base atletico stateless → _key_from_parts: distinct >1 → default suffix = most common → \"atletico-mg\" (or pr?) → in known_keys ✓ → returns default (most matches). Query \"atletico pr\" → (\"atletico\",\"pr\") → \"atletico-pr\" ✓. Query \"Athletico\" → cleaned \"athletico\" → not in TEAM_ALIASES? It IS: \"athletico\": (\"atletico\",\"pr\") ✓.\n\nNicknames: \"fla\" → NICKNAMES → (\"flamengo\",\"rj\") → key \"flamengo-rj\" ✓ in known keys ✓.\n\nNow `resolve` fuzzy: candidates dict maps cleaned candidate → key. `lowered` — candidates keys are already lowercase (clean_name produces lowercase; display_name(display) cleaned → lowercase ✓). OK.\n\nPotential issue: `variants()` returns variant display names for a base — used by find_team. Also `sibling_keys(\"flamengo-rj\")` → base \"flamengo\" partition: \"flamengo-rj\".rpartition(\"-\") → (\"flamengo\", \"-\", \"rj\") ✓ → siblings [\"flamengo-pi\"] ✓.\n\n`sibling_keys(\"corinthians\")` → rpartition(\"-\") on \"corinthians\" → (\"\", \"\", \"corinthians\") → suffix \"corinthians\", base \"\" → base \"\" not in suffix_counts → return [] ✓.\n\nNow fix clean_name. Also one more consideration in `_strip_ec_fc`: \"botafogo fc\"?? BRF has \"Botafogo SP\"/\"Botafogo RJ\" — with states ✓ no strip needed. FIFA \"Boavista FC\" is players-context (no strip) ✓. What about match-name \"Santos FC\"? Not present. OK.\n\nAlso \"Guarani FC\"? not present. Fine.\n\nLet me apply the clean_name fix.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0592a21d5001tozy0pDT9AE8EE","sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","messageID":"msg_05929a4a1001s4rGaJEAYt0C32"}}
