88+2\".split(\"+\")[0]))` = int(float(\"88\")) = 88 ✓. Actually both branches work. It's just ugly. Let me clean it up anyway... it works; leave for now but simplify later if linting. Actually let me fix it now for clarity.\n\nAlso FIFA \"Jersey Number\" is in FIFA_INT_COLUMNS (unused var — remove it) and used via parse_int inline ✓. Remove the unused constant.\n\nAlso `time=dt.split(\" \")[1] if \" \" in dt else None` — dt could be \"NA\" → no space → None ✓; \"2012-05-19 18:30:00\" → \"18:30:00\" ✓.\n\nBRF time \"20:00:00\" ✓.\n\nOne issue: `_load_br_football` season from date[:4] — if date is None/empty → parse_int(\"\") → None ✓.\n\nNow — a subtle registry issue: `registry.observe()` is called on raw display names, and `_variant_counts[base][clean_name(raw)]`. For base extraction during observe, aliases apply. E.g., \"Atlético Mineiro - MG\" (cup data) → alias via TEAM_ALIASES?? cleaned \"atletico mineiro - mg\" — not in TEAM_ALIASES (has suffix) → suffix split → base \"atletico mineiro\", state \"mg\" → context matches → _strip_ec_fc no → BASE_ALIASES no → observe counts suffix \"mg\" under base \"atletico mineiro\"!! But FIFA \"Atlético Mineiro\" (players ctx) → TEAM_ALIASES → (\"atletico\",\"mg\") → key \"atletico-mg\". And cup \"Atlético Mineiro - MG\" → canonical_key: same decompose path → base \"atletico mineiro\" state \"mg\" → _key_from_parts(\"atletico mineiro\", \"mg\") — suffix_counts for \"atletico mineiro\" = {\"mg\": n} → distinct ≤1 → key = \"atletico mineiro\" ≠ \"atletico-mg\"!!! BUG: \"Atlético Mineiro - MG\" in cup data maps to key \"atletico mineiro\" while \"Atletico-MG\" maps to \"atletico-mg\".\n\nLet me check: does cup data contain \"Atlético Mineiro - MG\"? From the collisions list earlier: 'Atlético - MG' appears (base atletico ✓), and I saw 'Atlético Mineiro - MG' in the collisions: `atletico mineiro: ['Atletico Mineiro', 'Atlético Mineiro - MG']` — YES it does (Copa do Brasil data). And plain \"Atletico Mineiro\" (BR-Football) → TEAM_ALIASES → atletico-mg ✓. So I MUST handle \"atletico mineiro - mg\" → (\"atletico\",\"mg\").\n\nFix: in `_decompose`, after suffix split, check `base in TEAM_ALIASES` (any context) and apply with state default. Let me restructure _decompose:\n\n```python\nbase, state, country = _split_suffix(cleaned)\nif base in TEAM_ALIASES:\n    alias_base, alias_state = TEAM_ALIASES[base]\n    base = alias_base\n    state = state or alias_state\n```\nThis applies for both contexts ✓. For \"atletico mineiro - mg\" → base \"atletico mineiro\" state \"mg\" → alias base \"atletico\", state = \"mg\" (already set) ✓ → key atletico-mg ✓. For plain \"atletico mineiro\" (matches ctx, BRF) → alias (\"atletico\",\"mg\") ✓. \n\nWait but careful: TEAM_ALIASES entries with state=None like \"vasco\"→(\"vasco da gama\",None): \"Vasco-RJ\"?? cleaned \"vasco rj\" → suffix split → base \"vasco\", state \"rj\" → alias: base=\"vasco da gama\", state = \"rj\" (stays) ✓ good.\n\nAnd \"santos fc\" (if ever) → alias (\"santos\",\"sp\") ✓.\n\nEdge conflict: alias state vs extracted state mismatch: \"América - RN\"?? base \"america\" not in aliases ✓ unaffected. \"america fc minas gerais\"? not a case. OK.\n\nAlso similar problem for BASE_ALIASES in _decompose: handled with state guard ✓.\n\nNow also `_decompose` order issue: the initial `if cleaned in TEAM_ALIASES` check handles full names without suffix; the post-split check handles names with suffix. Both needed ✓.\n\nAnother related bug: `canonical_key(context=\"players\")` re-checks TEAM_ALIASES/BASE_ALIASES — now redundant since _decompose handles it for all contexts. Simplify: remove the players-context re-check in canonical_key (keep context only for EC/FC strip). Actually the players block in canonical_key:\n```python\nif context == \"players\":\n    if base in TEAM_ALIASES: ...\n```\nNow unnecessary — _decompose covers it. Remove.\n\nAlso, another thing to verify: `registry.observe` uses context=\"matches\" always — for match data ✓. Players canonicalized AFTER finalize() ✓ (needs suffix_counts).\n\nOne more potential issue: FIFA clubs not in match data — e.g. \"Paris Saint-Germain\" → base \"paris saint germain\" (not observed) → key = base ✓. FIFA \"Botafogo\" → base botafogo stateless → _key_from_parts → distinct {rj,pb,sp} > 1 → default = most common state = rj → \"botafogo-rj\" ✓.\n\nFIFA \"Grêmio\" → base \"gremio\" → distinct {rs} → key \"gremio\" ✓.\n\nNow also think: `observe` counts suffix per base — but for base \"atletico mineiro\" (pre-fix bug) — after fix, \"atletico mineiro - mg\" observes under base \"atletico\" suffix \"mg\" ✓ consistent.\n\nLet me now also double check `_split_suffix` on \"santa rita - al\"? → base \"santa rita\", state \"al\" ✓. On \"rb brasil\"? BRF \"Red Bull Brasil\"? cleaned \"red bull brasil\" — trailing \"brasil\"? 3-letter country code is \"bra\" not \"brasil\" ✓ no split. On \"ldu\" → no separator match ✓. On \"abc rn\" → base \"abc\" state rn ✓. On \"psfc\"? fine.\n\nEdge: \"paysandu pa\" ✓. \"remo pa\" ✓. \"river pi\"?? \"Ríver - PI\" → base \"river\", state \"pi\" ✓ (Brazilian River-PI!). And \"river plate uru\" → base \"river plate\" country \"uru\" ✓ distinct bases \"river\" vs \"river plate\" ✓.\n\nHmm — \"River - PI\" base \"river\": also plain \"River Plate\" base \"river plate\" — fine.\n\nWhat about \"guarani (par)\" — paren with country ✓ → base \"guarani\", country \"par\" → registry guarani {sp, ce, par} → keys guarani-sp, guarani-ce, guarani-par ✓.\n\nNow fix _decompose and canonical_key.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0592b220b001PtAy68TPrQ7HCE","sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","messageID":"msg_0592a9dd6001BK8NVuxatSV5gz"}}
