pplied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py\n@@ -77,16 +77,34 @@\n }\n \n POSITION_WORDS = {\n     \"gk\": \"GK\", \"goalkeeper\": \"GK\", \"keeper\": \"GK\", \"goleiro\": \"GK\",\n-    \"def\": \"DEF\", \"defender\": \"DEF\", \"defense\": \"DEF\", \"defender?\": \"DEF\",\n+    \"def\": \"DEF\", \"defender\": \"DEF\", \"defense\": \"DEF\",\n     \"zagueiro\": \"DEF\", \"back\": \"DEF\", \"fullback\": \"DEF\",\n     \"mid\": \"MID\", \"midfielder\": \"MID\", \"midfield\": \"MID\", \"meia\": \"MID\",\n     \"fw\": \"FWD\", \"fwd\": \"FWD\", \"forward\": \"FWD\", \"forwards\": \"FWD\",\n     \"striker\": \"FWD\", \"attacker\": \"FWD\", \"winger\": \"FWD\", \"atacante\": \"FWD\",\n     \"center forward\": \"FWD\",\n }\n \n+NATIONALITY_WORD_MAP = {\n+    \"brazilian\": \"brazil\",\n+    \"argentinian\": \"argentina\",\n+    \"argentine\": \"argentina\",\n+    \"english\": \"england\",\n+    \"spanish\": \"spain\",\n+    \"french\": \"france\",\n+    \"german\": \"germany\",\n+    \"italian\": \"italy\",\n+    \"portuguese\": \"portugal\",\n+    \"dutch\": \"netherlands\",\n+    \"colombian\": \"colombia\",\n+    \"uruguayan\": \"uruguay\",\n+    \"chilean\": \"chile\",\n+    \"mexican\": \"mexico\",\n+    \"american\": \"united states\",\n+}\n+\n _STAGE_ALIASES = {\n     \"final\": \"final\",\n     \"finals\": \"final\",\n     \"finals (both legs)\": \"final\",\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py\n@@ -77,16 +77,34 @@\n }\n \n POSITION_WORDS = {\n     \"gk\": \"GK\", \"goalkeeper\": \"GK\", \"keeper\": \"GK\", \"goleiro\": \"GK\",\n-    \"def\": \"DEF\", \"defender\": \"DEF\", \"defense\": \"DEF\", \"defender?\": \"DEF\",\n+    \"def\": \"DEF\", \"defender\": \"DEF\", \"defense\": \"DEF\",\n     \"zagueiro\": \"DEF\", \"back\": \"DEF\", \"fullback\": \"DEF\",\n     \"mid\": \"MID\", \"midfielder\": \"MID\", \"midfield\": \"MID\", \"meia\": \"MID\",\n     \"fw\": \"FWD\", \"fwd\": \"FWD\", \"forward\": \"FWD\", \"forwards\": \"FWD\",\n     \"striker\": \"FWD\", \"attacker\": \"FWD\", \"winger\": \"FWD\", \"atacante\": \"FWD\",\n     \"center forward\": \"FWD\",\n }\n \n+NATIONALITY_WORD_MAP = {\n+    \"brazilian\": \"brazil\",\n+    \"argentinian\": \"argentina\",\n+    \"argentine\": \"argentina\",\n+    \"english\": \"england\",\n+    \"spanish\": \"spain\",\n+    \"french\": \"france\",\n+    \"german\": \"germany\",\n+    \"italian\": \"italy\",\n+    \"portuguese\": \"portugal\",\n+    \"dutch\": \"netherlands\",\n+    \"colombian\": \"colombia\",\n+    \"uruguayan\": \"uruguay\",\n+    \"chilean\": \"chile\",\n+    \"mexican\": \"mexico\",\n+    \"american\": \"united states\",\n+}\n+\n _STAGE_ALIASES = {\n     \"final\": \"final\",\n     \"finals\": \"final\",\n     \"finals (both legs)\": \"final\",\n","additions":19,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py","time":{"start":1788202594465,"end":1788202594467}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Issues to fix in queries.py:\n\n1. `_cup_final_round` logic bug: \n```python\nfinal_round = None\nfor round_number in sorted(rounds, reverse=True):\n    if rounds[round_number] <= 2:\n        final_round = round_number\n    break\n```\nThe `break` is outside the if — so it only checks the MAX round: if max round count ≤ 2 → final = max round; else None. For 2021: rounds {1:40,2:20,3:32,4:16}, max=4 count 16 > 2 → final=None ✓. For 2019: max=8 count 2 → final=8 ✓. For 2012: max=6 count 2 → final=6 ✓. Correct — but written confusingly (the break makes the loop single-iteration). Simplify to direct check.\n\n2. `search_players` club_key=None handling: if `club` given but `_resolve_club` returns None (empty)? `_resolve_club` raises or returns key; empty string guarded by `str(club).strip()` check before. OK. But `club_players` calls `search_players(club=club, limit=None)` — `results[:max(0, limit)]` with limit=None → max(0, None) TypeError! Fix: `if limit is not None: results = results[:max(0,limit)]`.\n\n3. `find_team`: `variants(key)` — registry.variants uses base of key; fine.\n\n4. In `search_matches`, when `team` given and `opponent` given, venue filter doesn't apply (venue only meaningful without opponent — actually venue could apply to the team perspective... if team=Flamengo opponent=Fluminense venue=home → Flamengo home matches vs Flu. My code applies venue only in the else branch (team without opponent). Let me apply venue in both cases — move venue checks outside the opponent branch:\n\n```python\nif team_key is not None:\n    if team_key not in (home, away): continue\n    if venue home and match.home_key != team_key: continue\n    if venue away and match.away_key != team_key: continue\nif opponent_key is not None:\n    if opponent_key not in (home, away): continue\n    if {home, away} != {team_key, opponent_key}: continue\n```\n\n5. `_resolve_position`: `POSITION_WORDS.get(cleaned)` — keys are already lowercase clean strings ✓ (\"center forward\" has a space — clean_name keeps spaces ✓). The redundant second loop over POSITION_WORDS is unnecessary — remove.\n\nAlso \"defender?\" entry in POSITION_WORDS is a typo artifact — remove.\n\n6. `statistics` biggest_away logic: if no away win exists, biggest_away.goal diff ≤ 0 → None ✓.\n\n7. `competition_overview`: builds `seasons` from all_sources=True but `match_count` uses `self._iter_matches([target], season=season, all_sources=True)` — counts all matches of that competition (filtered by season if given) ✓.\n\n8. `search_players` nationality: `_normalize_nationality(\"Brazilian\")` → \"brazil\" ✓; \"Brazil\" → \"brazil\" ✓. \"Argentina\" → \"argentina\" ✓; \"Argentinian\" → \"argentin\" ✗!! \"argentinian\".endswith(\"ian\") → strip \"ian\" → \"argentin\" ≠ \"argentina\". Hmm. Special-case: nationality matching should try exact first, then suffix-stripped. Better approach: compare both raw-cleaned AND suffix-stripped forms on both sides:\n\n```python\ndef _nationality_match(query_norm, player_norm):\n    return query_norm == player_norm or strip_suffix(query_norm) == player_norm or query_norm == strip_suffix(player_norm) ...\n```\nSimpler: normalize both sides with same function and ALSO compare with a small mapping for common adjectival forms. Cleanest: try candidates: [cleaned, cleaned-without-suffix] matched against player side similarly:\n\n```python\ndef _nationality_keys(value):\n    cleaned = clean_name(value)\n    keys = {cleaned}\n    for suffix in (\"ian\",\"an\",\"ese\",\"ine\"):\n        if cleaned.endswith(suffix) and len(cleaned) > len(suffix)+2:\n            keys.add(cleaned[:-len(suffix)])\n            keys.add(cleaned[:-len(suffix)] + \"a\")  # argentin → argentina\n    return keys\n```\nThen match if player keys ∩ query keys. \"argentinian\" → {argentinian, argentin, argentina} ∩ \"argentina\" ✓. \"brazilian\" → {brazilian, brazil} ∩ \"brazil\" ✓. \"english\" → \"english\"/\"engl\"? player side \"England\" → {england}; no match — acceptable (FIFA uses \"England\"; user should use \"England\"). Add \"english\"→\"england\", \"spanish\"→\"spain\", \"french\"→\"france\", \"german\"→\"germany\", \"italian\"→\"italy\", \"portuguese\"→\"portugal\", \"dutch\"→\"netherlands\", \"brazilian\"→\"brazil\" to a small map. Good enough.\n\n9. `search_matches` — when both date bounds and unplayed (date None) matches: date None excluded when bounds set ✓ reasonable.\n\n10. `head_to_head` limit default 10 — spec shows recent matches + counts. OK.\n\n11. `standings` sort tiebreak: (points, wins, GD, GF) desc — for 2019: Palmeiras 74 (21W) vs Santos 74 (22W) → Santos 2nd ✓ matches spec (Santos 2nd, Palmeiras 3rd).\n\n12. In `_apply_stage_filter`, `stage_note` logic is convoluted and possibly buggy: if filtered empty and included competitions intersect supports_stage → no note (falls through, stage_note stays None — wait: `elif stage_note is None:` then checks competitions_scanned from matches with comp in supports_stage; if empty sets a generic note. If non-empty → note stays None (fine, means stage data exists but no matches at that stage). Hmm — actually if the user asked stage=final for Libertadores+ Copa and there ARE such matches but they got filtered out by other criteria... edge case, skip. Let me simplify: after filtering, if not filtered:\n- if original matches had any Libertadores/Copa matches → note \"No matches at stage X found within these filters.\"\n- else → note \"Stage filters apply only to Copa Libertadores and Copa do Brasil.\"\n\n13. `list_teams` — displays sorted by count desc then name ✓.\n\n14. `DerbyResult.derby: object` — type it properly with `from brazilian_soccer_mcp.derbies import Derby` — but derbies.py imports clean_name from normalize — no circularity with queries. Import Derby at top of queries for the dataclass annotation. Actually `from __future__ import annotations` makes annotations strings — no runtime import needed, but let me import for clarity anyway... derbies.py imports from normalize only ✓ no cycle. I'll import at top and use `Derby` type.\n\n15. `find_data_dir` — checks candidates list; CWD walk ✓.\n\n16. `get_engine(data_dir)` ignores data_dir on subsequent calls (singleton) — fine for server; tests use fixture.\n\n17. `QueryError` for unknown competition message lists ALL_COMPETITIONS with accents — fine.\n\n18. `search_matches` limit: `matches[:max(0, limit)]` ✓.\n\n19. club_players returns all (limit=None) — fix slicing.\n\nLet me apply these fixes.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0592e3097001Y6eNiKzZ7XQnLa","sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","messageID":"msg_0592d9d46001Rba6QAu6qXY0Gu"}}
