s claim. The spec only demands standings \"calculated from match results\" — we calculate them from the data as provided. The incompleteness note covers this. But mislabeled extra matches could make a team's W/D/L exceed 38... For the champion question \"Who won 2023?\" the answer would be Grêmio (wrong; real was Palmeiras) BUT flagged \"season incomplete, leader shown\". Meh.\n\nLet me check the damage more precisely — count pairs meeting >2 times in 2023 \"Serie A\". If it's just a handful, I could add a league-consistency filter: for league competitions (Série A/B/C), drop matches between pairs that have already met twice in the same season (keeping first two by date)? That's principled: Brazilian Série A is strictly double round-robin (except 2016 Chapecoense exception!). Hmm, 2016: Chapecoense's last match wasn't played (round 38) — that's a MISSING match, not extra. The pair-count filter only drops EXTRAS (pair meeting 3+ times). Would it drop legitimate matches? Serie A fixtures never happen 3 times in a season. For 2003-2005 (24/22 teams) still double round-robin ✓. So the filter is safe for league competitions and removes source mislabels.\n\nBut careful: pair-count filter must consider PRIMARY source matches only... the mislabeled CdB matches ARE in the primary source (BRF is sole 2023 source). Filter algorithm per (competition ∈ Série A/B/C, season): group by unordered pair (home_key, away_key); if a pair appears ≥3 times, keep... which 2? The two with distinct venues (one home, one away per team ideally). Mislabel case: São Paulo x Palmeiras appears 3× (two CdB + one Serie A? or two Serie A + one CdB?). Ugh, ambiguity about WHICH 2 to keep. Wrong keeps corrupt W/D/L.\n\nLet me look at the actual data before deciding. Print pairs with >2 meetings in 2023 \"Serie A\" (primary only), and also check whether the true round-robin structure is recoverable. Also check other seasons for such anomalies (2014-2022 BRF is non-primary so wouldn't matter; novo/BM are clean).\n\nActually — wait. Also check: maybe those extra matches exist because BRF \"Serie A\" 2023 rows include both CdB semis AND the real league fixtures are all there. Palmeiras: 43 = 38 league + 5 mislabeled (2 Tombense + 2 São Paulo CdB + 1 more?). Let me count pairs.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05930d79f001eToUgFqrqAOHXe","sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","messageID":"msg_059305a99001sAbfOvHoy0zr90"}}
