2016 379 played? Earlier \"BM empty goals 82\" included 2016 Chapecoense + 2022 rows. So yes BM 2016 = 379 played, novo 380 (novo lists the match as... novo's 2016: does it have the Chapecoense match? Real world: the Chapecoense vs Atlético-MG round 38 match of 2016 was NOT played (post-plane-crash) — the CBF officially canceled it. novo 2016 has 380 rows — with what for that match? If novo recorded it as played with a fabricated score, novo is WRONG. Let me check novo 2016 Chapecoense round 38.\n\nActually the real 2016 final standings: Palmeiras champion 78 pts. Let me check what standings 2016 gives under each source. My engine now uses novo for 2016 — let me verify the result is still correct (Palmeiras 78, champion). If novo fabricated the canceled match, standings would differ from reality.\n\n2. **Copa do Brasil 2021: primary=BRF (111) instead of CUP (108)** — my 0.9-tolerance rule should have picked CUP (higher priority): 108 ≥ 0.9×111=99.9 ✓ → CUP... but it picked BRF! Why? OH — the bug: SOURCE_PRIORITY order is [BM, CUP, NOVO, LIB, BRF] — loop over SOURCE_PRIORITY checking counts: BM 0, CUP 108 ≥ 99.9 ✓ → primary = CUP. But output says BRF?! Let me check... unless CUP 2021 played count is NOT 108. Earlier raw count said CUP 2021 = 108 matches (rounds 1-4: 40+20+32+16=108) — how many have goals? 16 unplayed in CUP total! Maybe the 16 unplayed CUP rows are all 2021 (dataset exported before 2021 CdB finished — rounds 3/4 were mid-2021)! So CUP 2021 played might be ~92 < 99.9 → skipped → BRF (111, all played) primary. That's actually CORRECT behavior — more played data wins. OK good, not a bug.\n\nBut hmm — CdB 2021 primary = BRF (no rounds) → \"Copa do Brasil 2021 finals\" won't be found (BRF has no rounds, and my `_cup_final_round` only looks at SOURCE_CUP rows). Also 2022/2023 BRF-only. Fine — finals are findable for 2012-2020.\n\nHmm wait, actually let me reconsider the CUP 2021 case: CUP file has 2021 rounds 1-4 (with some unplayed), BRF has 111 played for 2021. Are they the same matches? BRF 111 > CUP 108 → BRF includes more (maybe CdB 2021 R16/QF that CUP file lacks). OK BRF primary for 2021 is fine.\n\n3. Now the 2016 question. Let me check the Chapecoense 2016 match in novo and what the standings say.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05935122b001s6mvUo0e1atAgo","sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","messageID":"msg_05934bbe4001qiPQMIsVAQJwJw"}}
