{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788203171478,"sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_cd070e3eccd744e7af3739df","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","newString":"    def observe(self, raw: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Record one occurrence of a team name from the match data.\"\"\"\n        base, state, country = self._decompose(raw, context=\"matches\")\n        if not base:\n            return\n        suffix = state or country\n        self._suffix_counts[base][suffix] += 1\n        self._variant_counts[base][str(raw).strip()] += 1","oldString":"    def observe(self, raw: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Record one occurrence of a team name from the match data.\"\"\"\n        base, state, country = self._decompose(raw, context=\"matches\")\n        if not base:\n            return\n        suffix = state or country\n        self._suffix_counts[base][suffix] += 1\n        self._variant_counts[base][clean_name(raw)] += 1"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -199,9 +199,9 @@\n     if not base:\n         return\n     suffix = state or country\n     self._suffix_counts[base][suffix] += 1\n-    self._variant_counts[base][clean_name(raw)] += 1\n+    self._variant_counts[base][str(raw).strip()] += 1\n \n def finalize(self) -> None:\n     self._known_keys = set(self.iter_keys())\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -199,9 +199,9 @@\n     if not base:\n         return\n     suffix = state or country\n     self._suffix_counts[base][suffix] += 1\n-    self._variant_counts[base][clean_name(raw)] += 1\n+    self._variant_counts[base][str(raw).strip()] += 1\n \n def finalize(self) -> None:\n     self._known_keys = set(self.iter_keys())\n \n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788203171473,"end":1788203171476}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The server works nicely. A few refinements:\n\n1. `statistics(competition=\"Brasileirão\", season=2019)` gives 952 matches — because \"Brasileirão\" resolves to ALL three series! 952 = 380 (A) + 378 (B) + 194 (C). For statistics this might surprise users asking about \"the Brasileirão\". But it's defensible: \"Brasileirão\" = all divisions. The label says \"(Brasileirão, 2019)\" — hmm, could add \"(all divisions)\" note when generic. Let me make `_resolve_competition` return a note when generic \"brasileirão\" resolved to 3 divisions, and format_statistics includes it. Actually simpler: when the query is generic and multiple comps resolved, the formatter can note \"including Série A, B and C\". Let me add a `generic` note.\n\n2. list_competitions shows \"14755 matches\" for Série A — that's ALL sources (all_sources=True in overview). Maybe show primary count? The overview is about data availability — showing all-source counts is fine but 14755 vs actual 380/season might confuse. I'll show both? Keep simple: show total rows (all sources) — it's the \"dataset coverage\" view. Actually let me make it clearer: \"matches (all sources)\". Hmm — or count primary: 21 seasons × ~390 = ~7950... I'll label it explicitly.\n\n3. Copa do Brasil 2021 season shown but finals not detectable there — fine.\n\n4. The `search_players` title \"Players from Brazilian\" — slightly awkward; \"from Brazil\" would be better. Minor: nationality display — keep as given. Eh, fine.\n\n5. Also noticed: `find_team` variants shows cleaned names (\"corinthians sp\") not original display names (\"Corinthians-SP\"). Better to show raw display variants. The registry `_variant_counts` keys are clean_name(raw) — I should store the RAW name instead. Let me change variants to record raw display names (with original accents/case) — more useful. In `observe`, record `str(raw).strip()` as variant (not cleaned).\n\n6. `club_players` for Fluminense shows fictional-ish names (FIFA 19 uses real players with slight name mangling for Brazilian clubs not fully licensed — \"Laure Santeiro\" is actually a scrambled name FIFA uses for unlicensed Brazilian league players!). Interesting data quirk — the FIFA dataset scrambled names for Brazilian league players. That's the dataset's nature (FIFA 19 had generic names for Brasileirão players). Nothing to do about it — it's the data.\n\nLet me apply refinements 1, 2, 5.\n\nFor 1: `_resolve_competition` returns (comps, note) — comp_note is already in MatchSearchResult but unused in formatting. Let me add the note to format_search_matches and format_statistics. Simplest: have the server pass competition + note. Actually — engine.statistics doesn't return the note. Let me add a `competition_scope` param to format_statistics that describes scope. I'll compute the scope label in the server tool: if competition given and resolved to multiple → append \"(all divisions)\". Let me expose `engine.resolve_competition_scope(competition) -> str` helper returning a display label like \"Brasileirão (Séries A, B, C)\" or just the competition name.\n\nSimplest: in server tools, compute `scope_label`:\n\n```python\ndef _comp_scope(engine, competition):\n    if not competition: return None\n    comps, _ = engine._resolve_competition(competition)\n    if len(comps) > 1: return f\"{competition} (all divisions: {', '.join(comps)})\"\n    return comps[0]\n```\n\nUse in statistics/biggest_wins/team_stats formatting. I'll add a public method `competition_label(competition)` on the engine.\n\nFor 2: format_competitions — change \"matches\" to show primary count: I'll add both: \"X matches in primary sources (Y total rows)\". Let me compute primary count in overview.\n\nFor 5: variants with raw names.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05936fe89001TMSWJNN0jAwec6","sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","messageID":"msg_05936a296001ajJOdaFLdFkYLM"}}
