{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788203190895,"sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_991677770beb4036b6a2ba0e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","newString":"    def _fuzzy_candidates(self) -> dict[str, str]:\n        candidates: dict[str, str] = {}\n        for key in self._known_keys:\n            candidates.setdefault(key, key)\n        for base, counts in self._variant_counts.items():\n            for variant in counts:\n                candidates.setdefault(clean_name(variant), self.canonical_key(variant))\n        for key, counts in self._display_counts.items():\n            for display in counts:\n                candidates.setdefault(clean_name(display), key)\n        return candidates","oldString":"    def _fuzzy_candidates(self) -> dict[str, str]:\n        candidates: dict[str, str] = {}\n        for key in self._known_keys:\n            candidates.setdefault(key, key)\n        for base, counts in self._variant_counts.items():\n            for variant in counts:\n                candidates.setdefault(variant, self._key_from_parts(base, self._default_suffix(base)))\n        for key, counts in self._display_counts.items():\n            for display in counts:\n                candidates.setdefault(clean_name(display), key)\n        return candidates"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -280,9 +280,9 @@\n for key in self._known_keys:\n     candidates.setdefault(key, key)\n for base, counts in self._variant_counts.items():\n     for variant in counts:\n-        candidates.setdefault(variant, self._key_from_parts(base, self._default_suffix(base)))\n+        candidates.setdefault(clean_name(variant), self.canonical_key(variant))\n for key, counts in self._display_counts.items():\n     for display in counts:\n         candidates.setdefault(clean_name(display), key)\n return candidates\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -280,9 +280,9 @@\n for key in self._known_keys:\n     candidates.setdefault(key, key)\n for base, counts in self._variant_counts.items():\n     for variant in counts:\n-        candidates.setdefault(variant, self._key_from_parts(base, self._default_suffix(base)))\n+        candidates.setdefault(clean_name(variant), self.canonical_key(variant))\n for key, counts in self._display_counts.items():\n     for display in counts:\n         candidates.setdefault(clean_name(display), key)\n return candidates\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788203190891,"end":1788203190893}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — `variants()` uses `counts.most_common()` from `_variant_counts[base]` and those keys are now RAW names ✓. But `resolve()` fuzzy candidates use `_variant_counts` keys via `candidates.setdefault(variant, ...)` — the lowered dict handles case ✓ but accents... `lowered = {c.lower(): k for c, k in candidates.items()}` — variant \"Corinthians-SP\" lowercased but not accent-stripped; query cleaned is accent-stripped (\"corinthians sp\" with space, not dash!). Hmm — \"corinthians-SP\" lower → \"corinthians-sp\" ≠ \"corinthians sp\". The suffix-split path in resolve handles that ✓; fuzzy candidates are the last resort — slight degradation is OK, but let me normalize candidate keys with clean_name for better matching:\n\nIn `_fuzzy_candidates`: `candidates.setdefault(clean_name(variant), key)` — but then `lowered` is redundant... `candidates` maps normalized → key. resolve does:\n```python\ncandidates = self._fuzzy_candidates()\nlowered = {c.lower(): k for c, k in candidates.items()}\n```\nIf candidates keys are clean_name'd, they're already lowercase — `lowered == candidates`. Then startswith/contains on cleaned query ✓. Let me update `_fuzzy_candidates` to clean variant keys. Also display names from `_display_counts` → clean them too.\n\nThen in resolve, the duplicate `lowered` mapping can just be `candidates`. Let me rewrite resolve's fuzzy section minimally: keep `lowered = {c.lower(): k ...}` (no-op for cleaned keys but harmless). Actually if two variants clean to the same key (e.g. \"Grêmio\" and \"Gremio RS\"→ different bases...) — setdefault keeps first; acceptable.\n\nUpdate `_fuzzy_candidates`:\n```python\ndef _fuzzy_candidates(self) -> dict[str, str]:\n    candidates: dict[str, str] = {}\n    for key in self._known_keys:\n        candidates.setdefault(key, key)\n    for base, counts in self._variant_counts.items():\n        default_key = self._key_from_parts(base, self._default_suffix(base))\n        for variant in counts:\n            candidates.setdefault(clean_name(variant), default_key)\n    for key, counts in self._display_counts.items():\n        for display in counts:\n            candidates.setdefault(clean_name(display), key)\n    return candidates\n```\n\nHmm wait — variant keys map to `default_key` (base or base-default-suffix)? E.g. variant \"Palmeiras-SP\" (base palmeiras, single suffix → key \"palmeiras\") ✓. Variant \"Fluminense\" (base fluminense, ambiguous {rj, pi} → default rj → \"fluminense-rj\") ✓ good. Variant \"Botafogo PB\" → base botafogo default rj → \"botafogo-rj\" ✗!! The variant \"Botafogo PB\" should map to botafogo-pb! Fix: map variant → key computed from the variant itself: `self.canonical_key(variant)` — canonical_key does the full decompose ✓:\n\n```python\nfor variant in counts:\n    candidates.setdefault(clean_name(variant), self.canonical_key(variant))\n```\n\ncanonical_key(\"Botafogo PB\") → base botafogo state pb → distinct>1 → \"botafogo-pb\" ✓. canonical_key(\"Fluminense\") → \"fluminense-rj\" ✓. \n\nSame for display names: `candidates.setdefault(clean_name(display), key)` ✓ (key already known).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059374a62001GIkl6Y1m3E3b05","sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","messageID":"msg_05937002d00197C5bRLrkb22OA"}}
