{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788203285095,"sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_825bdaf4984c48049871364a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Shared fixtures for the BDD test suite.\n\nThe engine loads all six CSV datasets once per test session (about one\nsecond), mirroring the single-load behaviour of the MCP server.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nREPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO_ROOT))\n\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.loader import load_data\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.queries import QueryEngine\n\nDATA_DIR = REPO_ROOT / \"data\" / \"kaggle\"\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef data_dir() -> Path:\n    return DATA_DIR\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef engine(data_dir) -> QueryEngine:\n    \"\"\"The query engine over all six datasets (loaded once).\"\"\"\n    return QueryEngine(load_data(data_dir))\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef registry(engine):\n    return engine.registry\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/tests/conftest.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-d0fbbb4f4ea5/tests/conftest.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"tests/conftest.py","time":{"start":1788203285087,"end":1788203285093}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now the BDD test suite. Per TASK.md: \"Use BDD (Behavior-Driven Development) test scenarios\" with Gherkin-style Given/When/Then structure in pytest.\n\nconftest.py: session-scoped engine fixture.\n\nTest files:\n1. `tests/test_normalization.py` — team name handling (spec: \"Handles team name variations correctly\")\n2. `tests/test_match_queries.py` — Feature: Match Queries\n3. `tests/test_team_queries.py` — Feature: Team Queries\n4. `tests/test_player_queries.py` — Feature: Player Queries\n5. `tests/test_competition_queries.py` — Feature: Competition Queries\n6. `tests/test_statistics.py` — Feature: Statistical Analysis\n7. `tests/test_mcp_server.py` — Feature: MCP Server integration\n8. `tests/test_performance.py` — performance budget\n\nEach test gets a Gherkin docstring and GWT structure. Let me write them with verified anchors:\n\n- 2019 Série A: Flamengo 90 pts (28W 6D 4L), Santos 74 (22W 8D 8L) 2nd, Palmeiras 74 (21W 11D 6L) 3rd, relegated bottom-4 = {Cruzeiro, CSA, Chapecoense, Avai} (order: points asc — Cruzeiro 36, CSA 32, Chapecoense 32, Avaí 20; relegated set check).\n- 2003: 24 teams, champion Cruzeiro.\n- 2022: Palmeiras top, 81 pts, note about incomplete.\n- Palmeiras 2022 Série A team stats: 38 matches 23W 12D 3L 64GF 27GA (BRF primary).\n- Corinthians home 2022: 19/12/4/3, 24/11.\n- 2019 Libertadores final: Flamengo 2-1 River Plate.\n- 2020 Libertadores final: Palmeiras 1-0 Santos.\n- Copa do Brasil finals: 2015 Santos vs Palmeiras in round 8; at least 18 final matches found (2 per season 2012-2020).\n- Fla-Flu: Brasileirão-only H2H = 43 matches; wins 17 Flamengo, draws 11, Fluminense 15 (per engine output: \"H2H Brasileirão: 43 matches: 17 - 11 - 15\" where order = a_wins - draws - b_wins). Let me hard-assert these.\n- Players: 827 Brazilians; Neymar 92 top; Fluminense roster 20; positions.\n- Gabriel Barbosa → TeamNotFoundError with suggestions.\n- Biggest wins Libertadores: River Plate 8-0 Jorge Wilstermann 2017.\n- Avg goals 2019 Série A = 2.3052... assert round 2.31 or abs(x-2.305)<0.01.\n- Statistics: 2019 Série A home win rate 48.4%.\n\nFor BDD style, I'll write tests like:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"\nFeature: Match Queries\n\nScenario: Find matches between two teams\n  Given the match data is loaded\n  When I search for matches between \"Flamengo\" and \"Fluminense\"\n  Then I should receive a list of matches\n  And each match should have date, scores, and competition\n\"\"\"\n\nclass TestFindMatchesBetweenTwoTeams:\n    def test_when_searching_matches_between_flamengo_and_fluminense_then_matches_have_date_scores_competition(self, engine):\n        # Given the match data is loaded\n        assert len(engine.matches) > 20_000\n        # When I search for matches between \"Flamengo\" and \"Fluminense\"\n        result = engine.search_matches(team=\"Flamengo\", opponent=\"Fluminense\")\n        # Then I should receive a list of matches\n        assert result.total >= 40\n        # And each match should have date, scores, and competition\n        ...\n```\n\nGiven/When/Then as comments + Gherkin docstring at module/class level. \n\nFor the server tests, use asyncio.run with the built server sharing the session engine.\n\nLet me write conftest and all test files now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05938ba59001DhCLQ2M7s1ymmR","sessionID":"ses_fa6e4b534ffex1G5nGEhqeGwzS","messageID":"msg_059386fcb001r0Viiq63ZGvS1L"}}
