ssol\" is close to \"palmeirass\" character-wise (both end in \"ss\"-ish sounds). \n\nOptions:\n1. Sort close matches by similarity and take the top one if it's meaningfully better than the rest: ratio(\"palmeirass\",\"palmeiras\")=0.941 vs ratio(\"palmeirass\",\"mirassol\")≈? matches... SequenceMatcher(\"palmeirass\",\"mirassol\") — common subsequence \"ira\"+\"ss\"?? ratio maybe 0.53?? But cutoff 0.6 passed... let me compute: probably ~0.6. A threshold rule: take best if best_ratio - second_ratio > 0.15 or best_ratio > 0.85.\n2. Change the test expectation (misspelling \"Palmeirass\" → suggestions, not resolution).\n\nOption 1 with guard: if best ratio ≥ 0.85 → resolve to best regardless. Implement:\n\n```python\nclose = difflib.get_close_matches(cleaned, known, n=3, cutoff=0.6)\nif close:\n    close_keys = {lowered[c] for c in close}\n    if len(close_keys) == 1:\n        return ...\n    ranked = sorted(close, key=lambda c: difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, cleaned, c).ratio(), reverse=True)\n    best = ranked[0]\n    if difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, cleaned, best).ratio() >= 0.85:\n        return lowered[best], display\nraise TeamNotFoundError(...)\n```\n\nratio(\"palmeirass\",\"palmeiras\") = 2×8/(9+8)?? wait: \"palmeirass\" (10 chars) vs \"palmeiras\" (9 chars): matching blocks = 8? ratio = 2*8/19 = 0.842... hmm that's < 0.85! Let me compute properly: SequenceMatcher(\"palmeirass\", \"palmeiras\") — the shorter is a prefix-substring of longer minus last 's'. matches = 9? \"palmeiras\" all 9 chars appear in order in \"palmeirass\" (\"palmeiras\" + \"s\"): actually \"palmeirass\" = p-a-l-m-e-i-r-a-s-s; \"palmeiras\" = p-a-l-m-e-i-r-a-s. The first 9 chars of \"palmeirass\" equal \"palmeiras\" ✓ → matches = 9 → ratio = 2*9/19 = 0.947 ✓ ≥ 0.85. Good.\n\nAnd \"mirassol\" ratio ~0.5-0.6. So rule works. Also for genuinely ambiguous typos (two similar club names), ratio < 0.85 → suggestions. \n\nLet me implement.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0593e513f0016gOa